{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019xeLWmub97KhtjBQucHdAM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"MAVEN Full Confusability Study\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"MAVEN Event Detection（168 event types, FrameNet hierarchy）的完整 confusability 研究：500-sample 重跑 count curve + within-count BCS 相关 + pairwise/per-type 双 embedding 分析 + confusion rate 分析。核心跨任务（NER→ED）验证。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"count_curve_relaxed_f1\": {\n7\t        \"count_1\": 0.098,\n8\t        \"count_6\": 0.112,\n9\t        \"count_12\": 0.155,\n10\t        \"count_22\": 0.192,\n11\t        \"count_44\": 0.238,\n12\t        \"count_64\": 0.241,\n13\t        \"count_100\": 0.243\n14\t      },\n15\t      \"count_curve_exact_f1\": {\n16\t        \"count_1\": 0.008,\n17\t        \"count_6\": 0.005,\n18\t        \"count_12\": 0.011,\n19\t        \"count_22\": 0.016,\n20\t        \"count_44\": 0.021,\n21\t        \"count_64\": 0.018\n22\t      },\n23\t      \"count_curve_recall_trend\": \"monotonically increasing 0.07→0.19 (opposite of Few-NERD)\",\n24\t      \"count_curve_precision_trend\": \"roughly flat 0.15-0.40, noisy\",\n25\t      \"within_count_bcs_f1\": {\n26\t        \"count_6\": {\n27\t          \"r\": 0.175,\n28\t          \"p\": 0.185,\n29\t          \"n\": 27,\n30\t          \"direction\": \"positive\",\n31\t          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n32\t        },\n33\t        \"count_12\": {\n34\t          \"r\": 0.124,\n35\t          \"p\": 0.315,\n36\t          \"n\": 27,\n37\t          \"direction\": \"positive\",\n38\t          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n39\t        },\n40\t        \"partial_pooled\": {\n41\t          \"r\": 0.142,\n42\t          \"p\": 0.108,\n43\t          \"n\": 54,\n44\t          \"direction\": \"positive\",\n45\t          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n46\t        }\n47\t      },\n48\t      \"pairwise_qwen3\": {\n49\t        \"pearson_r\": -0.009,\n50\t        \"pearson_p\": 0.38,\n51\t        \"n_pairs\": 14028,\n52\t        \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n53\t      },\n54\t      \"pairwise_minilm\": {\n55\t        \"pearson_r\": 0.115,\n56\t        \"pearson_p\": 2.1e-42,\n57\t        \"n_pairs\": 14028,\n58\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.128,\n59\t        \"nonzero_spearman_rho\": 0.185,\n60\t        \"verdict\": \"PASS\"\n61\t      },\n62\t      \"per_type_qwen3\": {\n63\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.195,\n64\t        \"p\": 0.018,\n65\t        \"direction\": \"positive_confounded\"\n66\t      },\n67\t      \"per_type_minilm\": {\n68\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.212,\n69\t        \"p\": 0.009,\n70\t        \"direction\": \"positive_confounded\"\n71\t      },\n72\t      \"confusion_rate_extreme\": {\n73\t        \"count_6_ratio\": 5.8,\n74\t        \"count_12_ratio\": 4.2\n75\t      },\n76\t      \"confusion_rate_random\": {\n77\t        \"count_6_ratio\": 1.4,\n78\t        \"count_12_ratio\": 1.3\n79\t      }\n80\t    },\n81\t    \"tables\": [\n82\t      \"Table: MAVEN Count Curve (500 samples, relaxed matching)\\n| Count | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | Recall | Precision | Pred/Gold |\\n|-------|-----------|----------|--------|-----------|-----------|\\n| 1     | 0.098     | 0.008    | 0.070  | 0.162     | 0.43      |\\n| 6     | 0.112     | 0.005    | 0.085  | 0.165     | 0.52      |\\n| 12    | 0.155     | 0.011    | 0.118  | 0.226     | 0.52      |\\n| 22    | 0.192     | 0.016    | 0.148  | 0.274     | 0.54      |\\n| 44    | 0.238     | 0.021    | 0.180  | 0.350     | 0.51      |\\n| 64    | 0.241     | 0.018    | 0.182  | 0.358     | 0.51      |\\n\",\n83\t      \"Table: MAVEN Within-Count BCS-F1 Correlation\\n| Count | r     | p     | Direction | Verdict |\\n|-------|-------|-------|-----------|---------|\\n| 6     | +0.175| 0.185 | positive  | FAIL    |\\n| 12    | +0.124| 0.315 | positive  | FAIL    |\\n| Pooled| +0.142| 0.108 | positive  | FAIL    |\\n\",\n84\t      \"Table: MAVEN Pairwise & Per-Type (2×2 embedding matrix)\\n|          | Pairwise r (p)         | Per-type ρ (p)       |\\n|----------|------------------------|----------------------|\\n| Qwen3    | -0.009 (0.38) ✗        | +0.195 (0.018) ✗     |\\n| MiniLM   | +0.115 (2.1e-42) ✓     | +0.212 (0.009) ✗     |\\n\"\n85\t    ],\n86\t    \"figures\": [],\n87\t    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN 结果确认 centrality confound 假说：在语义同质 schema 中，per-type 和 within-count batch-level 分析均被 confound。唯一存活的信号是 MiniLM pairwise (r=0.115)，但 Qwen3 pairwise 失败，且效应量小（r²=1.3%）。MAVEN 的 count curve 反转是对 SDGD 方法的致命打击——如果更多 types 在 prompt 中反而帮助模型，那么 decomposition（减少 types）必然降低性能。worst tier 叙事中，MAVEN 作为 \\\"centrality confound case study\\\" 仍有方法论价值，但不支持 SDGD 的前提假设。\\n\\n\\nMAVEN 的 168 event types 全部来自 FrameNet，同一语义域，导致 type embedding 分布高度同质。这造成三个后果：(1) count curve 反转——更多 types 为模型提供更 丰富的 event ontology 上下文，帮助模型理解每个 type 在 taxonomy 中的位置，因此 F1 随 count 增加而上升；(2) within-count BCS 相关为正方向——高 BCS batch 包含 语义中心的常见 event types（如 Killing, Attack, Movement），这些 types 在 training data 中频次高、定义清晰，LLM 本就擅长提取，因此高 BCS → 高 F1， 这是 centrality confound 而非 confusability 效应；(3) confusion rate 比 Few-NERD 低得多（5.8x vs 27.5x），因为 event trigger 本身是 verb/nominalization 而非 entity mention，type confusion 的表现形式不同（trigger 共享率高但不一定是 confusability 导致）。pairwise MiniLM 仍显著（r=0.115, p≈0），因为 n=14028 pair 提供了极大统计功效，即使效应量小也能检出——但这个 r 值比 Few-NERD 的 0.156 低， 且 Qwen3 pairwise 完全不显著，说明 pairwise 信号在同质 schema 上高度依赖 embedding 选择。\\n\"\n88\t  },\n89\t  {\n90\t    \"name\": \"DocRED Confusability Study\",\n91\t    \"description\": \"DocRED（96 relation types）上的 confusability 研究：count curve + BCS 相关分析。 文档级 RE 的 scaling stress test。\\n\",\n92\t    \"results\": {\n93\t      \"count_curve_f1\": {\n94\t        \"count_4\": 0.185,\n95\t        \"count_8\": 0.192,\n96\t        \"count_16\": 0.198,\n97\t        \"count_32\": 0.203,\n98\t        \"count_48\": 0.208,\n99\t        \"count_96\": 0.195\n100\t      },\n101\t      \"count_curve_trend\": \"near-flat with slight peak at count_48, no clear monotonic pattern\",\n102\t      \"within_count_bcs_f1\": {\n103\t        \"count_8\": {\n104\t          \"r\": 0.032,\n105\t          \"p\": 0.62,\n106\t          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n107\t        },\n108\t        \"count_16\": {\n109\t          \"r\": -0.058,\n110\t          \"p\": 0.48,\n111\t          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n112\t        },\n113\t        \"partial_pooled\": {\n114\t          \"r\": -0.015,\n115\t          \"p\": 0.84,\n116\t          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n117\t        }\n118\t      },\n119\t      \"pairwise_qwen3\": {\n120\t        \"pearson_r\": 0.023,\n121\t        \"pearson_p\": 0.14,\n122\t        \"n_pairs\": 4560,\n123\t        \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n124\t      },\n125\t      \"pairwise_minilm\": {\n126\t        \"pearson_r\": 0.031,\n127\t        \"pearson_p\": 0.08,\n128\t        \"n_pairs\": 4560,\n129\t        \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n130\t      },\n131\t      \"per_type_bcs_f1\": {\n132\t        \"spearman_rho\": -0.04,\n133\t        \"p\": 0.72,\n134\t        \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n135\t      },\n136\t      \"confusion_rate_extreme_ratio\": 1.8,\n137\t      \"overall_baseline_f1\": 0.195\n138\t    },\n139\t    \"tables\": [\n140\t      \"Table: DocRED Count Curve (document-level RE)\\n| Count | F1    | Recall | Precision | Confusion Rate |\\n|-------|-------|--------|-----------|---------------|\\n| 4     | 0.185 | 0.145  | 0.256     | 0.008         |\\n| 8     | 0.192 | 0.152  | 0.261     | 0.012         |\\n| 16    | 0.198 | 0.158  | 0.264     | 0.015         |\\n| 32    | 0.203 | 0.165  | 0.258     | 0.018         |\\n| 48    | 0.208 | 0.170  | 0.261     | 0.019         |\\n| 96    | 0.195 | 0.160  | 0.250     | 0.022         |\\n\"\n141\t    ],\n142\t    \"figures\": [],\n143\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED 结果是完全的 null result。confusability 假说在文档级 RE 上完全不成立。 worst tier 叙事中，DocRED 证明 confusability 效应受限于 sentence-level 任务—— 文档级任务中其他复杂度维度（跨句推理、entity pair 组合）占主导。如果论文要报告 此结果，需要 reframe 为 \\\"boundary condition\\\"：confusability 效应在 type definitions 占 prompt 显著比例的任务中才成立。但此实验为 P1，worst tier 下可能 不运行（10 天内优先 P0 实验），视为 supplementary material。\\n\\n\\nDocRED 是文档级 RE，每个样本包含多个句子和多个 entity pairs。性能瓶颈完全不在 type confusability 上，而在于：(1) 跨句推理能力——关系证据分散在多个句子中，LLM 需要 coreference 和 multi-hop reasoning；(2) entity pair 组合爆炸——文档中 n 个实体产生 O(n²) 个候选关系对，模型必须处理大量负样本；(3) 关系类型定义本身 依赖 entity type 约束（如 \\\"place_of_birth\\\" 要求 subject=person, object=location）， 这种结构化约束比 embedding 相似度更能预测性能。confusability 信号被这些更强的 因素完全淹没。count curve 近乎平坦，因为文档级 RE 的 prompt 长度主要由文档内容 （而非 type 定义）决定——96 个 relation type name 只占 prompt 的很小比例。\\n\"\n144\t  },\n145\t  {\n146\t    \"name\": \"Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\",\n147\t    \"description\": \"Few-NERD 上 {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS, high BCS} 的 2×2 因子设计。 检验 count 和 confusability 的交互效应（additive vs multiplicative）。\\n\",\n148\t    \"results\": {\n149\t      \"cell_means_f1\": {\n150\t        \"low_count_low_bcs\": 0.348,\n151\t        \"low_count_high_bcs\": 0.312,\n152\t        \"high_count_low_bcs\": 0.298,\n153\t        \"high_count_high_bcs\": 0.255\n154\t      },\n155\t      \"two_way_anova\": {\n156\t        \"count_main_effect\": {\n157\t          \"F\": 7.82,\n158\t          \"p\": 0.008,\n159\t          \"eta_sq\": 0.14,\n160\t          \"verdict\": \"SIGNIFICANT\"\n161\t        },\n162\t        \"bcs_main_effect\": {\n163\t          \"F\": 2.93,\n164\t          \"p\": 0.094,\n165\t          \"eta_sq\": 0.06,\n166\t          \"verdict\": \"MARGINAL\"\n167\t        },\n168\t        \"interaction\": {\n169\t          \"F\": 0.31,\n170\t          \"p\": 0.582,\n171\t          \"eta_sq\": 0.006,\n172\t          \"verdict\": \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n173\t        }\n174\t      },\n175\t      \"n_batches_per_cell\": 12,\n176\t      \"total_n\": 48,\n177\t      \"simple_effects\": {\n178\t        \"bcs_at_low_count\": {\n179\t          \"delta_f1\": -0.036,\n180\t          \"p\": 0.22\n181\t        },\n182\t        \"bcs_at_high_count\": {\n183\t          \"delta_f1\": -0.043,\n184\t          \"p\": 0.18\n185\t        }\n186\t      }\n187\t    },\n188\t    \"tables\": [\n189\t      \"Table: 2×2 Cell Means (F1, text_match)\\n|                | Low BCS     | High BCS    | BCS Effect |\\n|----------------|-------------|-------------|------------|\\n| Low Count (6)  | 0.348       | 0.312       | Δ=-0.036   |\\n| High Count (22)| 0.298       | 0.255       | Δ=-0.043   |\\n| Count Effect   | Δ=-0.050   | Δ=-0.057   |            |\\n\",\n190\t      \"Table: Two-Way ANOVA Results\\n| Source       | F     | p     | η²    | Verdict     |\\n|-------------|-------|-------|-------|-------------|\\n| Count        | 7.82  | 0.008 | 0.14  | Significant |\\n| BCS          | 2.93  | 0.094 | 0.06  | Marginal    |\\n| Count × BCS  | 0.31  | 0.582 | 0.006 | NS          |\\n\"\n191\t    ],\n192\t    \"figures\": [],\n193\t    \"analysis\": \"交互效应不显著是 worst tier 对 Claim 2（multi-channel degradation）的重大打击。 论文无法用 formal factorial design 证明两通道正交。只能退而求其次，基于 error taxonomy（exp-007）做 descriptive argument：count 降低 recall（omission）， confusability 增加 type confusion（substitution），两类错误机制不同→暗示正交。 但这种 descriptive 论证说服力远不如 significant interaction test。在 worst tier 叙事中，2×2 结果最多写一段文字报告 \\\"no significant interaction was detected, consistent with additive but not multiplicative independence\\\"。\\n\\n\\n2×2 设计的统计功效受限：每个 cell 约 12 个 batch，总 n=48。在这个样本量下， 检测交互效应需要 η²≥0.10 的大效应量。实际中，count 的主效应最强（η²=0.14）， 因为 count 直接影响 prompt 长度和 attention 分配，信号最清晰。BCS 主效应仅为 marginal（p=0.094），因为 batch-level BCS 与 F1 的关系本就受到 type frequency distribution 等 confound 的干扰——exp-002 已经表明 batch-level 信号远弱于 pairwise-level。交互效应完全不显著（p=0.582），说明 count 和 confusability 的 联合效应是（弱）加性的，不存在 multiplicative synergy。这在 worst tier 中意味 着论文只能声称 \\\"两个通道可能独立\\\" 但无法用 formal interaction test 支撑。\\n\"\n194\t  },\n195\t  {\n196\t    \"name\": \"Systematic Error Taxonomy by BCS Bins\",\n197\t    \"description\": \"对 Few-NERD exp-002 数据做系统 FP 分类（type_substitution / boundary_error / false_negative / hallucination），按 BCS bin 分析差异。机械层面支撑 multi-channel 模型。\\n\",\n198\t    \"results\": {\n199\t      \"error_distribution_overall\": {\n200\t        \"type_substitution_pct\": 0.18,\n201\t        \"boundary_error_pct\": 0.12,\n202\t        \"spurious_extraction_pct\": 0.45,\n203\t        \"missed_entity_pct\": 0.25\n204\t      },\n205\t      \"type_substitution_by_bcs\": {\n206\t        \"extreme_high_bcs_rate\": 0.058,\n207\t        \"extreme_low_bcs_rate\": 0.012,\n208\t        \"extreme_ratio\": 4.8,\n209\t        \"random_high_bcs_rate\": 0.022,\n210\t        \"random_low_bcs_rate\": 0.015,\n211\t        \"random_ratio\": 1.5\n212\t      },\n213\t      \"boundary_error_by_bcs\": {\n214\t        \"high_bcs_rate\": 0.041,\n215\t        \"low_bcs_rate\": 0.038,\n216\t        \"ratio\": 1.08,\n217\t        \"verdict\": \"NO_EFFECT\"\n218\t      },\n219\t      \"missed_entity_by_count\": {\n220\t        \"count_6_miss_rate\": 0.28,\n221\t        \"count_22_miss_rate\": 0.42,\n222\t        \"count_64_miss_rate\": 0.55,\n223\t        \"trend\": \"monotonically increasing with count\"\n224\t      },\n225\t      \"missed_entity_by_bcs\": {\n226\t        \"high_bcs_miss_rate\": 0.4,\n227\t        \"low_bcs_miss_rate\": 0.38,\n228\t        \"ratio\": 1.05,\n229\t        \"verdict\": \"NO_EFFECT\"\n230\t      },\n231\t      \"hallucination_rate\": 0.03,\n232\t      \"hallucination_by_bcs\": {\n233\t        \"verdict\": \"NO_EFFECT\"\n234\t      }\n235\t    },\n236\t    \"tables\": [\n237\t      \"Table: Error Distribution Overall\\n| Error Type          | Proportion | Primary Driver |\\n|---------------------|------------|----------------|\\n| Spurious Extraction | 45%        | Prompt format  |\\n| Missed Entity       | 25%        | Count (recall) |\\n| Type Substitution   | 18%        | BCS (confuse)  |\\n| Boundary Error      | 12%        | Span detection |\\n\",\n238\t      \"Table: Type Substitution Rate by BCS Condition\\n| Condition     | High BCS | Low BCS | Ratio |\\n|---------------|----------|---------|-------|\\n| Extreme Batch | 0.058    | 0.012   | 4.8x  |\\n| Random Batch  | 0.022    | 0.015   | 1.5x  |\\n\",\n239\t      \"Table: Missed Entity Rate by Count\\n| Count | Miss Rate | Δ vs Count_6 |\\n|-------|-----------|--------------|\\n| 6     | 0.28      | —            |\\n| 22    | 0.42      | +0.14        |\\n| 64    | 0.55      | +0.27        |\\n\"\n240\t    ],\n241\t    \"figures\": [],\n242\t    \"analysis\": \"Error taxonomy 部分支持 multi-channel 模型：(1) type substitution 受 BCS 影响 （extreme 4.8x），(2) missed entity 受 count 影响（monotonic）。但 worst tier 下两个弱点：(a) type substitution 只占总 error 的 18%，不是 dominant mode—— reviewer 会质疑 \\\"如果 confusability 只解释 18% 的 error，实际影响有多大？\\\"； (b) random batch ratio 仅 1.5x，远低于 extreme 的 4.8x——说明自然分布下效应 很小。论文只能做 descriptive analysis，不能做 formal causal claim。在 worst tier 叙事中，error taxonomy 作为 supporting evidence 放在 analysis section， 不作为独立 finding。\\n\\n\\nError taxonomy 的分类本身是 noisy 的——boundary error vs type substitution 的 区分依赖 text_match 容差设定。在 worst tier 下：(1) type substitution 在 extreme high-BCS batch 中确实更多（4.8x ratio），但 extreme batches 是刻意构造的极端 条件，random batches 中 ratio 仅 1.5x，实际场景中效应有限；(2) boundary error 不受 BCS 影响（ratio≈1.0），符合预期——boundary detection 是 span 层面的任务， 与 type confusability 无关；(3) missed entity（false negative）主要由 count 驱动（count_6 miss 28% vs count_64 miss 55%），不受 BCS 影响——支持 count→recall 通道；(4) 但整体 error 中 spurious extraction 占 45%，远超 type substitution 的 18%——这意味着 LLM 的主要问题是 \\\"提取不该提取的 span\\\" 而非 \\\"type 标错\\\"， confusability 只解释了一小部分 error。worst tier 的核心问题是：type confusion 不是 dominant error mode，因此 confusability 的实际影响被其他 error 源稀释。\\n\"\n243\t  },\n244\t  {\n245\t    \"name\": \"LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\",\n246\t    \"description\": \"用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复制 exp-002 protocol（Few-NERD, 25 random + extreme batches, count=6/12, pairwise + per-type 分析）。检验 confusability 效应的跨模型 泛化性。\\n\",\n247\t    \"results\": {\n248\t      \"baseline_f1_count64\": 0.378,\n249\t      \"baseline_vs_qwen3\": \"Δ=-3.6pp (Qwen3=0.414)\",\n250\t      \"pairwise_qwen3_embed\": {\n251\t        \"pearson_r\": 0.042,\n252\t        \"pearson_p\": 0.068,\n253\t        \"n_pairs\": 1953,\n254\t        \"verdict\": \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n255\t      },\n256\t      \"pairwise_qwen3_embed_nonzero\": {\n257\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.078,\n258\t        \"p\": 0.12,\n259\t        \"verdict\": \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n260\t      },\n261\t      \"per_type_bcs_f1\": {\n262\t        \"spearman_rho\": -0.082,\n263\t        \"p\": 0.538,\n264\t        \"n_types\": 58,\n265\t        \"partial_r_ctrl_logfreq\": -0.055,\n266\t        \"partial_p\": 0.684,\n267\t        \"verdict\": \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n268\t      },\n269\t      \"batch_f1_vs_bcs\": {\n270\t        \"count_6\": {\n271\t          \"r\": 0.108,\n272\t          \"p\": 0.42\n273\t        },\n274\t        \"count_12\": {\n275\t          \"r\": 0.185,\n276\t          \"p\": 0.21\n277\t        },\n278\t        \"partial_pooled\": {\n279\t          \"r\": 0.138,\n280\t          \"p\": 0.16\n281\t        }\n282\t      },\n283\t      \"confusion_rate_extreme\": {\n284\t        \"count_6_high\": 0.025,\n285\t        \"count_6_low\": 0.01,\n286\t        \"ratio_6\": 2.5,\n287\t        \"count_12_high\": 0.032,\n288\t        \"count_12_low\": 0.015,\n289\t        \"ratio_12\": 2.1\n290\t      },\n291\t      \"confusion_rate_random\": {\n292\t        \"count_6_ratio\": 1.2,\n293\t        \"count_12_ratio\": 1.15\n294\t      },\n295\t      \"cross_model_summary\": {\n296\t        \"qwen3_pairwise_r\": 0.156,\n297\t        \"llama_pairwise_r\": 0.042,\n298\t        \"qwen3_extreme_ratio\": \"10-28x\",\n299\t        \"llama_extreme_ratio\": \"2.1-2.5x\",\n300\t        \"qwen3_per_type_rho\": -0.293,\n301\t        \"llama_per_type_rho\": -0.082\n302\t      }\n303\t    },\n304\t    \"tables\": [\n305\t      \"Table: Cross-Model Comparison (Few-NERD)\\n| Metric                    | Qwen3-32B    | LLaMA-3.3-70B | Ratio    |\\n|---------------------------|-------------|---------------|----------|\\n| Baseline F1 (count_64)    | 0.414       | 0.378         | 0.91x    |\\n| Pairwise r (Qwen3 embed)  | 0.156***    | 0.042 (ns)    | 0.27x    |\\n| Per-type ρ                | -0.293*     | -0.082 (ns)   | 0.28x    |\\n| Extreme confusion ratio   | 10-28x      | 2.1-2.5x      | 0.10x    |\\n| Random confusion ratio    | 1.7-2.4x    | 1.15-1.2x     | 0.50x    |\\n\",\n306\t      \"Table: LLaMA Pairwise & Per-Type Statistics\\n| Analysis        | Statistic | Value  | p     | Verdict |\\n|-----------------|-----------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| Pairwise        | Pearson r | 0.042  | 0.068 | NS      |\\n| Pairwise NZ     | Spearman  | 0.078  | 0.120 | NS      |\\n| Per-type        | Spearman  | -0.082 | 0.538 | NS      |\\n| Per-type partial| Partial r | -0.055 | 0.684 | NS      |\\n\"\n307\t    ],\n308\t    \"figures\": [],\n309\t    \"analysis\": \"LLaMA 结果是 worst tier 中最关键的 negative result。cross_model_significant = 1 （仅 Qwen3），这意味着 confusability 效应可能是 Qwen3 特有的，而非 LLM IE 的 普遍现象。论文必须显著降级 Claim 1 的 generalizability：从 \\\"confusability independently predicts degradation in training-free LLM IE\\\" 改为 \\\"confusability sensitivity varies substantially across model families, with Qwen3 showing strong effects (r=0.156) and LLaMA showing weak/null effects (r=0.042)\\\"。在 worst tier 叙事中，这可 reframe 为解释力：\\\"prior conflicting findings about schema complexity may be partly explained by model-dependent confusability sensitivity\\\"——将缺陷转为贡献，但 reviewer 是否买账取决于写作。\\n\\n\\nLLaMA-3.3-70B 与 Qwen3-32B 在 confusability 敏感度上存在根本差异，原因可能是： (1) 模型规模差异——70B vs 32B，更大的模型有更大的 attention capacity，能更好地 处理 confusable types 的共现，因此 confusability 的 degradation 效应被缓解； (2) instruction tuning 差异——LLaMA-3.3 的 RLHF 训练可能更强调 precision 和 faithfulness，模型在不确定时倾向不输出（而非猜测相似 type），导致 type confusion error 本就少，confusability 信号弱；(3) internal representation 差异——LLaMA 的 embedding 空间对 Few-NERD types 的组织方式可能与 Qwen3 不同，Qwen3 embedding 中的 semantic proximity 模式不能直接迁移为 LLaMA 的 confusion 模式。\\npairwise r=0.042 (p=0.068) 在 α=0.05 下不显著但接近边界——这是最棘手的 结果：不能说完全无信号（p=0.068），但也不能声称显著。在 worst tier 叙事中， 这被 reframe 为 \\\"confusability effects are model-dependent, with effect size varying by 4x across model families (r=0.156 Qwen3 vs r=0.042 LLaMA)\\\"。confusion rate ratio 也大幅下降（2.5x vs Qwen3 的 27.5x），进一步说明 LLaMA 对 type confusion 更鲁棒。\\n\"\n310\t  },\n311\t  {\n312\t    \"name\": \"SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\",\n313\t    \"description\": \"Few-NERD 上的 SDGD-zero：Qwen3 embedding SCS + graph coloring (τ adaptive, k=1.0) 生成 confusability-minimizing batches，与 single-pass 对比。\\n\",\n314\t    \"results\": {\n315\t      \"graph_stats\": {\n316\t        \"threshold_tau\": 0.847,\n317\t        \"n_edges\": 142,\n318\t        \"edge_density\": 0.066,\n319\t        \"chromatic_number\": 8,\n320\t        \"avg_batch_size\": 8.25,\n321\t        \"max_batch_size\": 12,\n322\t        \"min_batch_size\": 4,\n323\t        \"max_intra_batch_bcs\": 0.842\n324\t      },\n325\t      \"sdgd_zero\": {\n326\t        \"f1\": 0.367,\n327\t        \"precision\": 0.318,\n328\t        \"recall\": 0.434,\n329\t        \"pred_gold_ratio\": 1.36\n330\t      },\n331\t      \"single_pass\": {\n332\t        \"f1\": 0.414,\n333\t        \"precision\": 0.648,\n334\t        \"recall\": 0.304\n335\t      },\n336\t      \"delta_f1_vs_single_pass\": -4.7,\n337\t      \"delta_precision\": -33.0,\n338\t      \"delta_recall\": 13.0,\n339\t      \"per_batch_f1_range\": [\n340\t        0.28,\n341\t        0.42\n342\t      ],\n343\t      \"per_batch_recall_range\": [\n344\t        0.35,\n345\t        0.52\n346\t      ],\n347\t      \"per_batch_precision_range\": [\n348\t        0.22,\n349\t        0.38\n350\t      ],\n351\t      \"merge_stats\": {\n352\t        \"total_predictions\": 4850,\n353\t        \"unique_predictions_after_dedup\": 4120,\n354\t        \"cross_batch_span_overlap\": 0.08,\n355\t        \"predictions_per_sample_avg\": 8.2,\n356\t        \"gold_per_sample_avg\": 5.9\n357\t      },\n358\t      \"api_calls\": \"8x single-pass (8000 vs 1000 for 1000 samples)\",\n359\t      \"wall_clock_multiplier\": 6.5\n360\t    },\n361\t    \"tables\": [\n362\t      \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass (Few-NERD, 66 types)\\n| Method      | F1    | Precision | Recall | Pred/Gold | API Calls |\\n|-------------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------|-----------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.648     | 0.304  | 0.47      | 1x        |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | 0.318     | 0.434  | 1.36      | 8x        |\\n| Δ           | -4.7pp| -33.0pp   | +13.0pp| +0.89     | +7x       |\\n\",\n363\t      \"Table: SDGD-zero Per-Batch Breakdown (top 4 batches)\\n| Batch | Types | Avg BCS | F1    | Recall | Precision |\\n|-------|-------|---------|-------|--------|-----------|\\n| 0     | 12    | 0.812   | 0.42  | 0.48   | 0.38      |\\n| 1     | 10    | 0.795   | 0.38  | 0.45   | 0.33      |\\n| 2     | 9     | 0.780   | 0.35  | 0.42   | 0.30      |\\n| 3     | 8     | 0.763   | 0.32  | 0.40   | 0.27      |\\n\"\n364\t    ],\n365\t    \"figures\": [],\n366\t    \"analysis\": \"SDGD-zero 的失败是 worst tier 的核心 negative result。直接否定 Claim 3。 failure mode 清晰且可解释：separating confusable types 剥夺了模型的 comparative disambiguation 能力。这是一个 informative negative result——它揭示了 LLM IE 中 type co-presence 的 dual role：(1) 增加 confusability（hypothesis 的前提）， (2) 提供 disambiguation context（SDGD 未预见的副作用）。在 worst tier 叙事中， 这个发现可以作为论文的一个 insight：\\\"confusability is a two-edged sword — the same type co-presence that causes confusion also enables disambiguation\\\"， 解释为什么简单的 separation strategy 不 work。但这最多放在 Discussion section， 不能作为 core contribution。\\n\\n\\nSDGD-zero 失败的核心机制是 \\\"disambiguation context loss\\\"。当 confusable types 被分到不同 batch 时，每个 batch 中的模型只看到 pair 的一端。例如 person-other 在 batch A，person-politician 在 batch B。处理含政治人物的句子时：\\n- Batch A（有 person-other，无 person-politician）：模型将政治人物标为\\n  person-other（因为这是最接近的可用 type）→ FP for person-other\\n- Batch B（有 person-politician，无 person-other）：模型将普通人标为\\n  person-politician（同理）→ FP for person-politician\\n\\nmerge 后，同一实体可能被两个 batch 分别标为不同 type（cross-batch span overlap 8%），评估时只有一个是 TP，另一个是 FP。更严重的是，每个 batch 只有 ~8 types， 模型倾向过度提取（pred/gold=1.36 vs single-pass 的 0.47），precision 从 0.648 暴跌到 0.318。recall 确实从 0.304 提升到 0.434（smaller batch → 更多 attention 给每个 type），但 precision 损失远大于 recall 增益。\\nF1 = 0.367 比 single-pass 的 0.414 低 4.7pp。SDGD 的前提假设（separating confusable types reduces confusion）是错误的——对 LLM 来说，看到 confusable types 的完整集合反而帮助 disambiguation。\\n\"\n367\t  },\n368\t  {\n369\t    \"name\": \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\",\n370\t    \"description\": \"MAVEN（168 event types）上的 SDGD-zero。用 adaptive threshold (k=1.0) 生成 confusability-minimizing batches。跨任务（NER→ED）验证 SDGD。\\n\",\n371\t    \"results\": {\n372\t      \"graph_stats\": {\n373\t        \"embedding\": \"qwen3\",\n374\t        \"scs_mean\": 0.216,\n375\t        \"scs_std\": 0.103,\n376\t        \"threshold_tau\": 0.319,\n377\t        \"n_edges\": 1850,\n378\t        \"edge_density\": 0.132,\n379\t        \"chromatic_number\": 15,\n380\t        \"avg_batch_size\": 11.2,\n381\t        \"min_batch_size\": 5,\n382\t        \"max_batch_size\": 18\n383\t      },\n384\t      \"sdgd_zero\": {\n385\t        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.168,\n386\t        \"exact_f1\": 0.012,\n387\t        \"relaxed_recall\": 0.13,\n388\t        \"relaxed_precision\": 0.238\n389\t      },\n390\t      \"single_pass\": {\n391\t        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.241,\n392\t        \"exact_f1\": 0.018\n393\t      },\n394\t      \"delta_relaxed_f1\": -7.3,\n395\t      \"api_calls\": \"15x single-pass\",\n396\t      \"wall_clock_multiplier\": 12.8\n397\t    },\n398\t    \"tables\": [\n399\t      \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass (MAVEN, 168 types)\\n| Method      | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\\n|-------------|-----------|----------|-----------|------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.241     | 0.018    | 1x        | 1x         |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | 0.012    | 15x       | 12.8x      |\\n| Δ           | -7.3pp    | -0.6pp   | +14x      | +11.8x     |\\n\"\n400\t    ],\n401\t    \"figures\": [],\n402\t    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN SDGD-zero 是最差的结果之一。15x API cost 换来 -7.3pp 性能下降。 与 Few-NERD 的 SDGD 失败共同构成 Claim 3 的致命反证：SDGD 在两个任务上 都差于 single-pass，且效果 consistent（方向一致、机制相同）。在 worst tier 叙事中，SDGD 相关实验（exp-008, 009, 010, 011, 013, 014）全部降级为 appendix 中的 negative result case study，正文仅用 1-2 段文字总结 \\\"we also explored confusability-minimizing decomposition, which failed because...\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMAVEN 上 SDGD-zero 失败更严重（Δ=-7.3pp vs Few-NERD 的 -4.7pp），原因： (1) MAVEN count curve 是上升的——更多 types 帮助模型理解 event ontology， decomposition 直接损害这个优势；(2) adaptive τ=0.319（因 MAVEN Qwen3 SCS 分布集中在低值区间），graph 中 edge density=13.2%，coloring 产生 15 个 batch， 每个约 11 types——这比 single-pass 的 168 types 少了 93%的 type 上下文； (3) 15 个 batch 意味着 15x API 调用，wall-clock 12.8x 但性能反而更差—— cost-quality 全面恶化；(4) MAVEN event trigger 是 verb/nominalization，多个 event type 共享同一 trigger word（如 \\\"attack\\\" 可以是 Attack 也可以是 Conflict）， 模型需要看到完整 event taxonomy 才能正确 assign type。\\n\"\n403\t  },\n404\t  {\n405\t    \"name\": \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\",\n406\t    \"description\": \"Few-NERD 上的 SDGD-cal：用 5-10 calibration examples 构建 empirical confusion matrix，替代 embedding SCS。与 SDGD-zero 和 single-pass 对比。\\n\",\n407\t    \"results\": {\n408\t      \"calibration_stats\": {\n409\t        \"n_calibration_samples\": 8,\n410\t        \"calibration_api_calls\": 8,\n411\t        \"empirical_confusion_pairs_nonzero\": 85,\n412\t        \"spearman_vs_embedding_scs\": 0.125,\n413\t        \"p_vs_embedding_scs\": 0.031\n414\t      },\n415\t      \"graph_stats\": {\n416\t        \"threshold_tau\": \"adaptive on empirical confusion\",\n417\t        \"n_edges\": 62,\n418\t        \"chromatic_number\": 7,\n419\t        \"avg_batch_size\": 9.4\n420\t      },\n421\t      \"sdgd_cal\": {\n422\t        \"f1\": 0.381,\n423\t        \"precision\": 0.342,\n424\t        \"recall\": 0.43,\n425\t        \"pred_gold_ratio\": 1.26\n426\t      },\n427\t      \"comparison\": {\n428\t        \"vs_single_pass_delta\": -3.3,\n429\t        \"vs_sdgd_zero_delta\": 1.4,\n430\t        \"vs_random_delta\": 0.7,\n431\t        \"vs_random_p\": 0.58\n432\t      },\n433\t      \"single_pass_f1\": 0.414,\n434\t      \"sdgd_zero_f1\": 0.367,\n435\t      \"random_f1\": 0.374\n436\t    },\n437\t    \"tables\": [\n438\t      \"Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (Few-NERD)\\n| Method      | F1    | Δ vs SP | Precision | Recall | API Overhead   |\\n|-------------|-------|---------|-----------|--------|----------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.414 | —       | 0.648     | 0.304  | 1x             |\\n| Random (k=8)| 0.374 | -4.0    | 0.335     | 0.425  | 8x             |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | -4.7    | 0.318     | 0.434  | 8x             |\\n| SDGD-cal    | 0.381 | -3.3    | 0.342     | 0.430  | 7x + 8 calib   |\\n\"\n439\t    ],\n440\t    \"figures\": [],\n441\t    \"analysis\": \"SDGD-cal 是 SDGD 方法线的 \\\"best effort\\\"——用 ground truth confusion 替代 proxy。 即使如此仍低于 single-pass 3.3pp。这最终否定了 confusability-minimizing decomposition 的整体方法路线：问题不在 confusion matrix 的质量，而在于 decomposition 本身损害了 LLM 的 disambiguation context。在 worst tier 叙事中， SDGD-cal 的 marginal improvement over SDGD-zero 可作为 exp-015（SCS validation） 的间接证据：embedding proxy 与 empirical confusion 仅弱相关（ρ=0.125），但这 不是失败的主因——即使 perfect confusion matrix 也不能拯救 decomposition strategy。\\n\\n\\nSDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 好（+1.4pp），因为 empirical confusion matrix 比 embedding SCS 更准确地反映实际 model confusion：(1) 非零 confusion pair 只有 85 对（vs embedding SCS 的 142 条 edge），graph 更稀疏 → 7 个 batch（vs 8 个），每个 batch 更大 → 更多 type 上下文；(2) calibration 捕捉到一些 embedding SCS 预测不 到的 confusion pattern（如语义不近但 surface form 相似的 type pair）。但 SDGD-cal 仍低于 single-pass 3.3pp，因为 decomposition 的核心问题（disambiguation context loss）不因 confusion matrix 质量改善而消失。与 random batching 的差异仅 +0.7pp (p=0.58)，不显著——confusability-aware grouping 即使用了 empirical data 也没有 显著优势。calibration 的额外 cost（8 次 API 调用）换来的 improvement 微乎其微。\\n\"\n442\t  },\n443\t  {\n444\t    \"name\": \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\",\n445\t    \"description\": \"MAVEN（168 types）上的 SDGD-cal：empirical confusion matrix + graph coloring。 Full comparison table。\\n\",\n446\t    \"results\": {\n447\t      \"calibration_stats\": {\n448\t        \"n_calibration_samples\": 10,\n449\t        \"empirical_confusion_pairs_nonzero\": 210\n450\t      },\n451\t      \"graph_stats\": {\n452\t        \"chromatic_number\": 12,\n453\t        \"avg_batch_size\": 14.0\n454\t      },\n455\t      \"sdgd_cal\": {\n456\t        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.188,\n457\t        \"exact_f1\": 0.014\n458\t      },\n459\t      \"comparison\": {\n460\t        \"vs_single_pass_delta\": -5.3,\n461\t        \"vs_sdgd_zero_delta\": 2.0,\n462\t        \"vs_random_delta\": 0.8,\n463\t        \"vs_random_p\": 0.62\n464\t      },\n465\t      \"single_pass_relaxed_f1\": 0.241,\n466\t      \"sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1\": 0.168,\n467\t      \"random_relaxed_f1\": 0.18\n468\t    },\n469\t    \"tables\": [\n470\t      \"Table: Full Comparison (MAVEN, 168 types, relaxed matching)\\n| Method      | Relaxed F1 | Δ vs SP | API Calls      |\\n|-------------|-----------|---------|----------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.241     | —       | 1x             |\\n| Random (k=12)| 0.180    | -6.1    | 12x            |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | -7.3    | 15x            |\\n| SDGD-cal    | 0.188     | -5.3    | 12x + 10 calib |\\n\"\n471\t    ],\n472\t    \"figures\": [],\n473\t    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN SDGD-cal 确认 decomposition 在 event detection 上全面失败。所有方法 均差于 single-pass，且 MAVEN 的差距（5-7pp）比 Few-NERD（3-5pp）更大。 这强化了 worst tier 的核心结论：decomposition 不是通用 solution，type co-presence 在很多场景中是 feature 而非 bug。\\n\\n\\n与 Few-NERD 相同模式：SDGD-cal 好于 SDGD-zero（+2.0pp）但仍远差于 single-pass （-5.3pp）。MAVEN 的 empirical confusion matrix 更密（210 nonzero pairs vs Few-NERD 的 85），因为 168 types 中很多 event type 确实会互相 confuse（尤其是 同一 FrameNet frame 下的 sibling types）。但 calibration 帮助有限——核心问题 仍然是 MAVEN 的性能与 type count 正相关，decomposition 损害性能。\\n\"\n474\t  },\n475\t  {\n476\t    \"name\": \"Random Batching Ablation\",\n477\t    \"description\": \"与 SDGD-zero 相同 batch 数量 k，随机分组。隔离 confusability-aware grouping 的价值（排除 batch count reduction 的贡献）。\\n\",\n478\t    \"results\": {\n479\t      \"fewnerd\": {\n480\t        \"random_f1\": 0.374,\n481\t        \"sdgd_zero_f1\": 0.367,\n482\t        \"delta_sdgd_vs_random\": -0.7,\n483\t        \"paired_t_p\": 0.68,\n484\t        \"n_random_seeds\": 10,\n485\t        \"random_f1_std\": 0.018,\n486\t        \"random_f1_range\": [\n487\t          0.348,\n488\t          0.402\n489\t        ],\n490\t        \"single_pass_f1\": 0.414\n491\t      },\n492\t      \"maven\": {\n493\t        \"random_relaxed_f1\": 0.18,\n494\t        \"sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1\": 0.168,\n495\t        \"delta_sdgd_vs_random\": -1.2,\n496\t        \"paired_t_p\": 0.42,\n497\t        \"n_random_seeds\": 5\n498\t      },\n499\t      \"interpretation\": {\n500\t        \"sdgd_vs_random_significant\": false,\n501\t        \"confusability_aware_grouping_benefit\": null\n502\t      }\n503\t    },\n504\t    \"tables\": [\n505\t      \"Table: Random vs SDGD-zero (Few-NERD, k=8)\\n| Method     | Mean F1 | Std   | Range         | vs Single-Pass |\\n|------------|---------|-------|---------------|----------------|\\n| Random×10  | 0.374   | 0.018 | [0.348,0.402] | -4.0pp         |\\n| SDGD-zero  | 0.367   | —     | —             | -4.7pp         |\\n| Δ (SDGD-Random) | -0.7pp | — | —           | p=0.68 (NS)    |\\n\",\n506\t      \"Table: Random vs SDGD-zero (MAVEN, k=15/12)\\n| Method     | Relaxed F1 | vs Single-Pass |\\n|------------|-----------|----------------|\\n| Random×5   | 0.180     | -6.1pp         |\\n| SDGD-zero  | 0.168     | -7.3pp         |\\n| Δ          | -1.2pp    | p=0.42 (NS)    |\\n\"\n507\t    ],\n508\t    \"figures\": [],\n509\t    \"analysis\": \"Random batching ablation 是 Claim 3 的 definitive kill shot。SDGD 不显著优于 random→confusability-aware grouping 无价值。combined with SDGD < single-pass→ decomposition 本身有害。Claim 3 完全不成立。在 worst tier 叙事中，这个实验 的 negative result 本身有教育意义：it demonstrates that the intuitive principle \\\"separate confusable types\\\" is wrong for LLM IE，因为 LLMs 使用 type co-presence 做 comparative reasoning。\\n\\n\\nRandom batching 在 10 个 random seeds 上平均 F1=0.374（std=0.018），而 SDGD-zero F1=0.367。SDGD 比 random 差 0.7pp（p=0.68），差异不显著。实际上 SDGD 可能略 差于 random，因为 SDGD 刻意将 confusable types 分开——这意味着每个 batch 内的 types 都是 semantically distant 的，模型缺乏同一 semantic cluster 的 types 作为 disambiguation anchor。Random batching 偶尔会把 confusable types 放在一起 （概率约 1/k），这些 batch 的 disambiguation 更好，平均下来 random 反而略优。\\n在 MAVEN 上同样：random F1=0.180 vs SDGD F1=0.168（Δ=-1.2pp, p=0.42）。 SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 不仅无益，可能有害。\\n\"\n510\t  },\n511\t  {\n512\t    \"name\": \"Per-Type Splitting (UniNER-style) Ablation\",\n513\t    \"description\": \"1 type per batch（k=66/168）。Decomposition 的上界。揭示 latency-quality tradeoff。\\n\",\n514\t    \"results\": {\n515\t      \"fewnerd\": {\n516\t        \"per_type_f1\": 0.33,\n517\t        \"per_type_precision\": 0.225,\n518\t        \"per_type_recall\": 0.62,\n519\t        \"api_calls\": \"66x single-pass\",\n520\t        \"wall_clock_multiplier\": 48.0\n521\t      },\n522\t      \"maven\": {\n523\t        \"per_type_relaxed_f1\": 0.108,\n524\t        \"api_calls\": \"168x single-pass\",\n525\t        \"wall_clock_multiplier\": 135.0\n526\t      },\n527\t      \"comparison_fewnerd\": {\n528\t        \"single_pass\": 0.414,\n529\t        \"sdgd_zero\": 0.367,\n530\t        \"random\": 0.374,\n531\t        \"per_type\": 0.33\n532\t      },\n533\t      \"ordering\": \"single-pass > random ≈ SDGD-zero > per-type\"\n534\t    },\n535\t    \"tables\": [\n536\t      \"Table: Full Method Comparison (Few-NERD)\\n| Method      | F1    | Precision | Recall | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\\n|-------------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------|------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.648     | 0.304  | 1x        | 1x         |\\n| SDGD-cal    | 0.381 | 0.342     | 0.430  | 7x        | 5.5x       |\\n| Random (k=8)| 0.374 | 0.335     | 0.425  | 8x        | 6.5x       |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | 0.318     | 0.434  | 8x        | 6.5x       |\\n| Per-type    | 0.330 | 0.225     | 0.620  | 66x       | 48x        |\\n\",\n537\t      \"Table: Full Method Comparison (MAVEN, relaxed)\\n| Method      | Relaxed F1 | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\\n|-------------|-----------|-----------|------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.241     | 1x        | 1x         |\\n| SDGD-cal    | 0.188     | 12x       | 10x        |\\n| Random      | 0.180     | 12x       | 10x        |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | 15x       | 12.8x      |\\n| Per-type    | 0.108     | 168x      | 135x       |\\n\"\n538\t    ],\n539\t    \"figures\": [],\n540\t    \"analysis\": \"Per-type ablation 完成了 decomposition failure 的完整图景。方法排序 single-pass > random ≈ SDGD > per-type 说明：(1) decomposition granularity 与 F1 反相关；(2) type co-presence 是 net positive（disambiguation > confusion）； (3) SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 不提供额外价值（≈ random）。 在 worst tier 叙事中，这个结果可 reframe 为 empirical finding：\\\"LLM IE benefits from full schema visibility; type co-presence enables comparative reasoning that outweighs confusability-induced errors\\\"——这本身是一个有价值 的 insight，但不是 method contribution。\\n\\n\\nPer-type splitting 是 decomposition 的极端形式：每个 batch 只有 1 个 type。 这完全消除 type confusion（BCS=0），但也完全消除 disambiguation context。\\nFew-NERD 结果（F1=0.330）几乎等于 exp003a count_1 的 F1=0.323——符合预期， 因为 per-type extraction 本质就是 count=1。precision 极低（0.225）因为模型 只知道一个 type，会把任何像样的 span 都标为该 type（massive over-extraction）。 recall 最高（0.620）因为模型 aggressively 搜索这个 type 的所有 instance。\\nMAVEN 更惨（relaxed F1=0.108），因为 MAVEN 的 count_1 relaxed_F1 就只有 0.098。 168x API 调用使 wall-clock time 完全不可接受。\\n排序 single-pass > random ≈ SDGD > per-type 证明：decomposition granularity 与性能成反比。batch 越大越好（更多 type context），单pass 最优。\\n\"\n541\t  },\n542\t  {\n543\t    \"name\": \"Embedding SCS vs Empirical Confusion Validation\",\n544\t    \"description\": \"计算 embedding SCS（Qwen3 / MiniLM）与 empirical confusion matrix 之间的 rank correlation。验证 embedding proxy 对实际 model confusion 的预测力。\\n\",\n545\t    \"results\": {\n546\t      \"qwen3_scs_vs_empirical\": {\n547\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.125,\n548\t        \"p\": 0.031,\n549\t        \"kendall_tau\": 0.092,\n550\t        \"p_kendall\": 0.044,\n551\t        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 85\n552\t      },\n553\t      \"minilm_scs_vs_empirical\": {\n554\t        \"spearman_rho\": 0.098,\n555\t        \"p\": 0.082,\n556\t        \"kendall_tau\": 0.071,\n557\t        \"p_kendall\": 0.115,\n558\t        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 85\n559\t      },\n560\t      \"top_confused_pair_scs_rank\": {\n561\t        \"person_other_politician\": {\n562\t          \"scs_rank\": 3,\n563\t          \"confusion_rank\": 1\n564\t        },\n565\t        \"building_other_library\": {\n566\t          \"scs_rank\": 45,\n567\t          \"confusion_rank\": 8,\n568\t          \"comment\": \"high confusion, low SCS — embedding 未捕捉的 confusion pattern\"\n569\t        }\n570\t      },\n571\t      \"scs_false_positive_rate\": 0.42,\n572\t      \"scs_false_negative_rate\": 0.35\n573\t    },\n574\t    \"tables\": [\n575\t      \"Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation\\n| Embedding | Spearman ρ | p     | Kendall τ | p     |\\n|-----------|-----------|-------|-----------|-------|\\n| Qwen3     | 0.125     | 0.031 | 0.092     | 0.044 |\\n| MiniLM    | 0.098     | 0.082 | 0.071     | 0.115 |\\n\",\n576\t      \"Table: SCS Proxy Error Analysis\\n| Metric              | Qwen3 | MiniLM |\\n|---------------------|-------|--------|\\n| False Positive Rate | 0.42  | 0.48   |\\n| False Negative Rate | 0.35  | 0.40   |\\n| Top-1 Match         | Yes   | No     |\\n\"\n577\t    ],\n578\t    \"figures\": [],\n579\t    \"analysis\": \"SCS validation 结果解释了 SDGD 失败的一个次要原因（proxy 质量差），但不是主因 （主因是 decomposition 本身有害）。ρ=0.125 说明 embedding SCS 只能解释 ~1.6% 的 confusion variance——作为 graph 构建的基础远远不够。即使用 empirical confusion (exp-010 SDGD-cal) 也只比 random 好 0.7pp（不显著），所以 proxy 质量不是瓶颈。 在 worst tier 叙事中，SCS validation 作为 methodological finding 报告： \\\"embedding-based confusability proxies have limited predictive power for actual model confusion patterns, suggesting that confusability is mediated by factors beyond semantic similarity\\\"——这对未来工作有指导价值。\\n\\n\\nEmbedding SCS 与 empirical confusion 仅弱相关（ρ=0.125），原因：(1) embedding similarity 反映 semantic proximity，但 model confusion 还受 surface form similarity、type definition wording、in-context position 等因素影响——这些因素 与 embedding space 正交；(2) SCS 是对称的（sim(A,B)=sim(B,A)），但实际 confusion 是非对称的（person-other → person-politician 的概率可能远高于反向）；(3) 42% 的 false positive rate 意味着 SCS 预测为 confusable 的 type pair 中近一半实际 不被 confuse——这些 false alarm 导致 SDGD-zero 过度分离 types，graph 变密， batch 数量过多。\\nMiniLM SCS 更差（ρ=0.098, p=0.082），因为 MiniLM 是 general-purpose sentence embedding，不 align 到 Qwen3 的 internal representation。这解释了为什么 extraction model alignment 对 per-type signal 很重要（exp-002 中 Qwen3 per-type ρ=-0.293 vs MiniLM ρ≈0）。\\n\"\n580\t  },\n581\t  {\n582\t    \"name\": \"Cross-Experiment Summary (for paper narrative)\",\n583\t    \"description\": \"综合所有实验的 worst tier 结果，构建论文核心 tables 和 narrative。\\n\",\n584\t    \"results\": {\n585\t      \"claim1_pairwise_matrix\": {\n586\t        \"qwen3_fewnerd\": \"r=0.156*** ✓\",\n587\t        \"qwen3_maven\": \"r=-0.009 (ns) ✗\",\n588\t        \"qwen3_fewrel\": \"pending\",\n589\t        \"minilm_fewnerd\": \"not tested\",\n590\t        \"minilm_maven\": \"r=0.115*** ✓\",\n591\t        \"minilm_fewrel\": \"Δ=21-50pp ✓ (pilot)\",\n592\t        \"llama_fewnerd\": \"r=0.042 (ns) ✗\",\n593\t        \"significant_cells\": 3,\n594\t        \"total_cells\": 7,\n595\t        \"verdict\": \"partial — 3/7 significant, no single embedding/model universally works\"\n596\t      },\n597\t      \"claim2_evidence\": {\n598\t        \"count_recall_monotonic\": true,\n599\t        \"bcs_type_substitution_ratio_extreme\": \"4.8x\",\n600\t        \"bcs_type_substitution_ratio_random\": \"1.5x\",\n601\t        \"interaction_significant\": false,\n602\t        \"error_taxonomy_dominant_mode\": \"spurious extraction (45%), not type confusion (18%)\",\n603\t        \"verdict\": \"directional — channels exist but confusability channel is weak relative to other error sources\"\n604\t      },\n605\t      \"claim3_evidence\": {\n606\t        \"sdgd_zero_fewnerd\": \"F1=0.367, Δ=-4.7pp vs SP\",\n607\t        \"sdgd_zero_maven\": \"relF1=0.168, Δ=-7.3pp vs SP\",\n608\t        \"sdgd_cal_fewnerd\": \"F1=0.381, Δ=-3.3pp vs SP\",\n609\t        \"sdgd_cal_maven\": \"relF1=0.188, Δ=-5.3pp vs SP\",\n610\t        \"sdgd_vs_random_significant\": false,\n611\t        \"per_type_worst\": true,\n612\t        \"verdict\": \"FAILED — all decomposition methods inferior to single-pass\"\n613\t      },\n614\t      \"recommended_paper_structure\": [\n615\t        \"1. Introduction: 'What makes schemas complex for LLMs?'\",\n616\t        \"2. Related Work: decomposition approaches + empirical studies\",\n617\t        \"3. Experimental Setup: 3 tasks, 2 models, 2 embeddings\",\n618\t        \"4. Finding 1: Pairwise confusability predicts type confusion (model-dependent)\",\n619\t        \"5. Finding 2: Count and confusability act through distinguishable channels\",\n620\t        \"6. Finding 3: Per-type aggregation introduces centrality confound\",\n621\t        \"7. Finding 4: Confusability-minimizing decomposition fails (negative result)\",\n622\t        \"8. Discussion: implications for future work\",\n623\t        \"9. Conclusion\"\n624\t      ],\n625\t      \"recommended_venue\": \"EMNLP 2026 Findings (realistic), Main (stretch)\"\n626\t    },\n627\t    \"tables\": [\n628\t      \"Table: Pairwise SCS-Confusion Signal (Cross-Task × Cross-Model × Cross-Embedding)\\n| Model  | Embedding | Few-NERD (NER) | MAVEN (ED) | FewRel (RE) |\\n|--------|-----------|----------------|------------|-------------|\\n| Qwen3  | Qwen3     | r=0.156***     | r=-0.009   | —           |\\n| Qwen3  | MiniLM    | —              | r=0.115*** | Δ=21-50pp*  |\\n| LLaMA  | Qwen3     | r=0.042        | —          | —           |\\n*** p<0.001, * pilot only\\n\",\n629\t      \"Table: SDGD Full Comparison (worst tier)\\n| Method       | Few-NERD F1 | Δ vs SP | MAVEN relF1 | Δ vs SP |\\n|-------------|-------------|---------|-------------|---------|\\n| Single-pass  | 0.414       | —       | 0.241       | —       |\\n| SDGD-cal     | 0.381       | -3.3    | 0.188       | -5.3    |\\n| Random (=k)  | 0.374       | -4.0    | 0.180       | -6.1    |\\n| SDGD-zero    | 0.367       | -4.7    | 0.168       | -7.3    |\\n| Per-type     | 0.330       | -8.4    | 0.108       | -13.3   |\\n\"\n630\t    ],\n631\t    \"figures\": [],\n632\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 论文的核心卖点不是 positive findings 而是 systematic methodology 和 honest reporting。三个 takeaway：(1) confusability 信号存在但 model/embedding-dependent——未来工作不能假设 universal confusability measure； (2) per-type 聚合有 centrality confound——未来工作应使用 pairwise 分析； (3) confusability-minimizing decomposition 失败——LLM 需要 type co-presence 做 comparative reasoning，简单分离策略适得其反。这些 negative-but-informative results 加上 controlled experimental design 可以支撑一篇 Findings paper。\\n\\nWorst tier 总体图景：论文有两个可靠发现（pairwise confusability signal on Qwen3×FewNERD + MiniLM×MAVEN；centrality confound on MAVEN）和一系列 informative negative results（LLaMA 无信号、SDGD 全面失败、interaction 不显著）。叙事必须 从 \\\"we discover and exploit confusability\\\" 彻底转为 \\\"we systematically investigate schema complexity, finding that confusability effects are real but model-dependent, and that the intuitive decomposition strategy fails because LLMs need type co-presence for disambiguation\\\"。这种 \\\"honest empirical study with negative results\\\" 的论文在 EMNLP Findings 有先例（如 \\\"Do Prompt-Based Models Really Understand the Meaning of Their Prompts?\\\" ACL 2022），但需要极强的写作功力 和清晰的 takeaway。\\n\"\n633\t  }\n634\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d7a5a19-b1bd-4793-b072-30ea1d0ec2fd","uuid":"6ff45298-2c29-4061-b9e1-1be46157b77b","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:16:18.871Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_18/projects/schema-dag-extraction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T113743/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"MAVEN Full Confusability Study\",\n    \"description\": \"MAVEN Event Detection（168 event types, FrameNet hierarchy）的完整 confusability 研究：500-sample 重跑 count curve + within-count BCS 相关 + pairwise/per-type 双 embedding 分析 + confusion rate 分析。核心跨任务（NER→ED）验证。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"count_curve_relaxed_f1\": {\n        \"count_1\": 0.098,\n        \"count_6\": 0.112,\n        \"count_12\": 0.155,\n        \"count_22\": 0.192,\n        \"count_44\": 0.238,\n        \"count_64\": 0.241,\n        \"count_100\": 0.243\n      },\n      \"count_curve_exact_f1\": {\n        \"count_1\": 0.008,\n        \"count_6\": 0.005,\n        \"count_12\": 0.011,\n        \"count_22\": 0.016,\n        \"count_44\": 0.021,\n        \"count_64\": 0.018\n      },\n      \"count_curve_recall_trend\": \"monotonically increasing 0.07→0.19 (opposite of Few-NERD)\",\n      \"count_curve_precision_trend\": \"roughly flat 0.15-0.40, noisy\",\n      \"within_count_bcs_f1\": {\n        \"count_6\": {\n          \"r\": 0.175,\n          \"p\": 0.185,\n          \"n\": 27,\n          \"direction\": \"positive\",\n          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n        },\n        \"count_12\": {\n          \"r\": 0.124,\n          \"p\": 0.315,\n          \"n\": 27,\n          \"direction\": \"positive\",\n          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n        },\n        \"partial_pooled\": {\n          \"r\": 0.142,\n          \"p\": 0.108,\n          \"n\": 54,\n          \"direction\": \"positive\",\n          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"pairwise_qwen3\": {\n        \"pearson_r\": -0.009,\n        \"pearson_p\": 0.38,\n        \"n_pairs\": 14028,\n        \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n      },\n      \"pairwise_minilm\": {\n        \"pearson_r\": 0.115,\n        \"pearson_p\": 2.1e-42,\n        \"n_pairs\": 14028,\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.128,\n        \"nonzero_spearman_rho\": 0.185,\n        \"verdict\": \"PASS\"\n      },\n      \"per_type_qwen3\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.195,\n        \"p\": 0.018,\n        \"direction\": \"positive_confounded\"\n      },\n      \"per_type_minilm\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.212,\n        \"p\": 0.009,\n        \"direction\": \"positive_confounded\"\n      },\n      \"confusion_rate_extreme\": {\n        \"count_6_ratio\": 5.8,\n        \"count_12_ratio\": 4.2\n      },\n      \"confusion_rate_random\": {\n        \"count_6_ratio\": 1.4,\n        \"count_12_ratio\": 1.3\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: MAVEN Count Curve (500 samples, relaxed matching)\\n| Count | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | Recall | Precision | Pred/Gold |\\n|-------|-----------|----------|--------|-----------|-----------|\\n| 1     | 0.098     | 0.008    | 0.070  | 0.162     | 0.43      |\\n| 6     | 0.112     | 0.005    | 0.085  | 0.165     | 0.52      |\\n| 12    | 0.155     | 0.011    | 0.118  | 0.226     | 0.52      |\\n| 22    | 0.192     | 0.016    | 0.148  | 0.274     | 0.54      |\\n| 44    | 0.238     | 0.021    | 0.180  | 0.350     | 0.51      |\\n| 64    | 0.241     | 0.018    | 0.182  | 0.358     | 0.51      |\\n\",\n      \"Table: MAVEN Within-Count BCS-F1 Correlation\\n| Count | r     | p     | Direction | Verdict |\\n|-------|-------|-------|-----------|---------|\\n| 6     | +0.175| 0.185 | positive  | FAIL    |\\n| 12    | +0.124| 0.315 | positive  | FAIL    |\\n| Pooled| +0.142| 0.108 | positive  | FAIL    |\\n\",\n      \"Table: MAVEN Pairwise & Per-Type (2×2 embedding matrix)\\n|          | Pairwise r (p)         | Per-type ρ (p)       |\\n|----------|------------------------|----------------------|\\n| Qwen3    | -0.009 (0.38) ✗        | +0.195 (0.018) ✗     |\\n| MiniLM   | +0.115 (2.1e-42) ✓     | +0.212 (0.009) ✗     |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN 结果确认 centrality confound 假说：在语义同质 schema 中，per-type 和 within-count batch-level 分析均被 confound。唯一存活的信号是 MiniLM pairwise (r=0.115)，但 Qwen3 pairwise 失败，且效应量小（r²=1.3%）。MAVEN 的 count curve 反转是对 SDGD 方法的致命打击——如果更多 types 在 prompt 中反而帮助模型，那么 decomposition（减少 types）必然降低性能。worst tier 叙事中，MAVEN 作为 \\\"centrality confound case study\\\" 仍有方法论价值，但不支持 SDGD 的前提假设。\\n\\n\\nMAVEN 的 168 event types 全部来自 FrameNet，同一语义域，导致 type embedding 分布高度同质。这造成三个后果：(1) count curve 反转——更多 types 为模型提供更 丰富的 event ontology 上下文，帮助模型理解每个 type 在 taxonomy 中的位置，因此 F1 随 count 增加而上升；(2) within-count BCS 相关为正方向——高 BCS batch 包含 语义中心的常见 event types（如 Killing, Attack, Movement），这些 types 在 training data 中频次高、定义清晰，LLM 本就擅长提取，因此高 BCS → 高 F1， 这是 centrality confound 而非 confusability 效应；(3) confusion rate 比 Few-NERD 低得多（5.8x vs 27.5x），因为 event trigger 本身是 verb/nominalization 而非 entity mention，type confusion 的表现形式不同（trigger 共享率高但不一定是 confusability 导致）。pairwise MiniLM 仍显著（r=0.115, p≈0），因为 n=14028 pair 提供了极大统计功效，即使效应量小也能检出——但这个 r 值比 Few-NERD 的 0.156 低， 且 Qwen3 pairwise 完全不显著，说明 pairwise 信号在同质 schema 上高度依赖 embedding 选择。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED Confusability Study\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED（96 relation types）上的 confusability 研究：count curve + BCS 相关分析。 文档级 RE 的 scaling stress test。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"count_curve_f1\": {\n        \"count_4\": 0.185,\n        \"count_8\": 0.192,\n        \"count_16\": 0.198,\n        \"count_32\": 0.203,\n        \"count_48\": 0.208,\n        \"count_96\": 0.195\n      },\n      \"count_curve_trend\": \"near-flat with slight peak at count_48, no clear monotonic pattern\",\n      \"within_count_bcs_f1\": {\n        \"count_8\": {\n          \"r\": 0.032,\n          \"p\": 0.62,\n          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n        },\n        \"count_16\": {\n          \"r\": -0.058,\n          \"p\": 0.48,\n          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n        },\n        \"partial_pooled\": {\n          \"r\": -0.015,\n          \"p\": 0.84,\n          \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"pairwise_qwen3\": {\n        \"pearson_r\": 0.023,\n        \"pearson_p\": 0.14,\n        \"n_pairs\": 4560,\n        \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n      },\n      \"pairwise_minilm\": {\n        \"pearson_r\": 0.031,\n        \"pearson_p\": 0.08,\n        \"n_pairs\": 4560,\n        \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n      },\n      \"per_type_bcs_f1\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": -0.04,\n        \"p\": 0.72,\n        \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n      },\n      \"confusion_rate_extreme_ratio\": 1.8,\n      \"overall_baseline_f1\": 0.195\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: DocRED Count Curve (document-level RE)\\n| Count | F1    | Recall | Precision | Confusion Rate |\\n|-------|-------|--------|-----------|---------------|\\n| 4     | 0.185 | 0.145  | 0.256     | 0.008         |\\n| 8     | 0.192 | 0.152  | 0.261     | 0.012         |\\n| 16    | 0.198 | 0.158  | 0.264     | 0.015         |\\n| 32    | 0.203 | 0.165  | 0.258     | 0.018         |\\n| 48    | 0.208 | 0.170  | 0.261     | 0.019         |\\n| 96    | 0.195 | 0.160  | 0.250     | 0.022         |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED 结果是完全的 null result。confusability 假说在文档级 RE 上完全不成立。 worst tier 叙事中，DocRED 证明 confusability 效应受限于 sentence-level 任务—— 文档级任务中其他复杂度维度（跨句推理、entity pair 组合）占主导。如果论文要报告 此结果，需要 reframe 为 \\\"boundary condition\\\"：confusability 效应在 type definitions 占 prompt 显著比例的任务中才成立。但此实验为 P1，worst tier 下可能 不运行（10 天内优先 P0 实验），视为 supplementary material。\\n\\n\\nDocRED 是文档级 RE，每个样本包含多个句子和多个 entity pairs。性能瓶颈完全不在 type confusability 上，而在于：(1) 跨句推理能力——关系证据分散在多个句子中，LLM 需要 coreference 和 multi-hop reasoning；(2) entity pair 组合爆炸——文档中 n 个实体产生 O(n²) 个候选关系对，模型必须处理大量负样本；(3) 关系类型定义本身 依赖 entity type 约束（如 \\\"place_of_birth\\\" 要求 subject=person, object=location）， 这种结构化约束比 embedding 相似度更能预测性能。confusability 信号被这些更强的 因素完全淹没。count curve 近乎平坦，因为文档级 RE 的 prompt 长度主要由文档内容 （而非 type 定义）决定——96 个 relation type name 只占 prompt 的很小比例。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\",\n    \"description\": \"Few-NERD 上 {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS, high BCS} 的 2×2 因子设计。 检验 count 和 confusability 的交互效应（additive vs multiplicative）。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cell_means_f1\": {\n        \"low_count_low_bcs\": 0.348,\n        \"low_count_high_bcs\": 0.312,\n        \"high_count_low_bcs\": 0.298,\n        \"high_count_high_bcs\": 0.255\n      },\n      \"two_way_anova\": {\n        \"count_main_effect\": {\n          \"F\": 7.82,\n          \"p\": 0.008,\n          \"eta_sq\": 0.14,\n          \"verdict\": \"SIGNIFICANT\"\n        },\n        \"bcs_main_effect\": {\n          \"F\": 2.93,\n          \"p\": 0.094,\n          \"eta_sq\": 0.06,\n          \"verdict\": \"MARGINAL\"\n        },\n        \"interaction\": {\n          \"F\": 0.31,\n          \"p\": 0.582,\n          \"eta_sq\": 0.006,\n          \"verdict\": \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"n_batches_per_cell\": 12,\n      \"total_n\": 48,\n      \"simple_effects\": {\n        \"bcs_at_low_count\": {\n          \"delta_f1\": -0.036,\n          \"p\": 0.22\n        },\n        \"bcs_at_high_count\": {\n          \"delta_f1\": -0.043,\n          \"p\": 0.18\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: 2×2 Cell Means (F1, text_match)\\n|                | Low BCS     | High BCS    | BCS Effect |\\n|----------------|-------------|-------------|------------|\\n| Low Count (6)  | 0.348       | 0.312       | Δ=-0.036   |\\n| High Count (22)| 0.298       | 0.255       | Δ=-0.043   |\\n| Count Effect   | Δ=-0.050   | Δ=-0.057   |            |\\n\",\n      \"Table: Two-Way ANOVA Results\\n| Source       | F     | p     | η²    | Verdict     |\\n|-------------|-------|-------|-------|-------------|\\n| Count        | 7.82  | 0.008 | 0.14  | Significant |\\n| BCS          | 2.93  | 0.094 | 0.06  | Marginal    |\\n| Count × BCS  | 0.31  | 0.582 | 0.006 | NS          |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"交互效应不显著是 worst tier 对 Claim 2（multi-channel degradation）的重大打击。 论文无法用 formal factorial design 证明两通道正交。只能退而求其次，基于 error taxonomy（exp-007）做 descriptive argument：count 降低 recall（omission）， confusability 增加 type confusion（substitution），两类错误机制不同→暗示正交。 但这种 descriptive 论证说服力远不如 significant interaction test。在 worst tier 叙事中，2×2 结果最多写一段文字报告 \\\"no significant interaction was detected, consistent with additive but not multiplicative independence\\\"。\\n\\n\\n2×2 设计的统计功效受限：每个 cell 约 12 个 batch，总 n=48。在这个样本量下， 检测交互效应需要 η²≥0.10 的大效应量。实际中，count 的主效应最强（η²=0.14）， 因为 count 直接影响 prompt 长度和 attention 分配，信号最清晰。BCS 主效应仅为 marginal（p=0.094），因为 batch-level BCS 与 F1 的关系本就受到 type frequency distribution 等 confound 的干扰——exp-002 已经表明 batch-level 信号远弱于 pairwise-level。交互效应完全不显著（p=0.582），说明 count 和 confusability 的 联合效应是（弱）加性的，不存在 multiplicative synergy。这在 worst tier 中意味 着论文只能声称 \\\"两个通道可能独立\\\" 但无法用 formal interaction test 支撑。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Systematic Error Taxonomy by BCS Bins\",\n    \"description\": \"对 Few-NERD exp-002 数据做系统 FP 分类（type_substitution / boundary_error / false_negative / hallucination），按 BCS bin 分析差异。机械层面支撑 multi-channel 模型。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"error_distribution_overall\": {\n        \"type_substitution_pct\": 0.18,\n        \"boundary_error_pct\": 0.12,\n        \"spurious_extraction_pct\": 0.45,\n        \"missed_entity_pct\": 0.25\n      },\n      \"type_substitution_by_bcs\": {\n        \"extreme_high_bcs_rate\": 0.058,\n        \"extreme_low_bcs_rate\": 0.012,\n        \"extreme_ratio\": 4.8,\n        \"random_high_bcs_rate\": 0.022,\n        \"random_low_bcs_rate\": 0.015,\n        \"random_ratio\": 1.5\n      },\n      \"boundary_error_by_bcs\": {\n        \"high_bcs_rate\": 0.041,\n        \"low_bcs_rate\": 0.038,\n        \"ratio\": 1.08,\n        \"verdict\": \"NO_EFFECT\"\n      },\n      \"missed_entity_by_count\": {\n        \"count_6_miss_rate\": 0.28,\n        \"count_22_miss_rate\": 0.42,\n        \"count_64_miss_rate\": 0.55,\n        \"trend\": \"monotonically increasing with count\"\n      },\n      \"missed_entity_by_bcs\": {\n        \"high_bcs_miss_rate\": 0.4,\n        \"low_bcs_miss_rate\": 0.38,\n        \"ratio\": 1.05,\n        \"verdict\": \"NO_EFFECT\"\n      },\n      \"hallucination_rate\": 0.03,\n      \"hallucination_by_bcs\": {\n        \"verdict\": \"NO_EFFECT\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: Error Distribution Overall\\n| Error Type          | Proportion | Primary Driver |\\n|---------------------|------------|----------------|\\n| Spurious Extraction | 45%        | Prompt format  |\\n| Missed Entity       | 25%        | Count (recall) |\\n| Type Substitution   | 18%        | BCS (confuse)  |\\n| Boundary Error      | 12%        | Span detection |\\n\",\n      \"Table: Type Substitution Rate by BCS Condition\\n| Condition     | High BCS | Low BCS | Ratio |\\n|---------------|----------|---------|-------|\\n| Extreme Batch | 0.058    | 0.012   | 4.8x  |\\n| Random Batch  | 0.022    | 0.015   | 1.5x  |\\n\",\n      \"Table: Missed Entity Rate by Count\\n| Count | Miss Rate | Δ vs Count_6 |\\n|-------|-----------|--------------|\\n| 6     | 0.28      | —            |\\n| 22    | 0.42      | +0.14        |\\n| 64    | 0.55      | +0.27        |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Error taxonomy 部分支持 multi-channel 模型：(1) type substitution 受 BCS 影响 （extreme 4.8x），(2) missed entity 受 count 影响（monotonic）。但 worst tier 下两个弱点：(a) type substitution 只占总 error 的 18%，不是 dominant mode—— reviewer 会质疑 \\\"如果 confusability 只解释 18% 的 error，实际影响有多大？\\\"； (b) random batch ratio 仅 1.5x，远低于 extreme 的 4.8x——说明自然分布下效应 很小。论文只能做 descriptive analysis，不能做 formal causal claim。在 worst tier 叙事中，error taxonomy 作为 supporting evidence 放在 analysis section， 不作为独立 finding。\\n\\n\\nError taxonomy 的分类本身是 noisy 的——boundary error vs type substitution 的 区分依赖 text_match 容差设定。在 worst tier 下：(1) type substitution 在 extreme high-BCS batch 中确实更多（4.8x ratio），但 extreme batches 是刻意构造的极端 条件，random batches 中 ratio 仅 1.5x，实际场景中效应有限；(2) boundary error 不受 BCS 影响（ratio≈1.0），符合预期——boundary detection 是 span 层面的任务， 与 type confusability 无关；(3) missed entity（false negative）主要由 count 驱动（count_6 miss 28% vs count_64 miss 55%），不受 BCS 影响——支持 count→recall 通道；(4) 但整体 error 中 spurious extraction 占 45%，远超 type substitution 的 18%——这意味着 LLM 的主要问题是 \\\"提取不该提取的 span\\\" 而非 \\\"type 标错\\\"， confusability 只解释了一小部分 error。worst tier 的核心问题是：type confusion 不是 dominant error mode，因此 confusability 的实际影响被其他 error 源稀释。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复制 exp-002 protocol（Few-NERD, 25 random + extreme batches, count=6/12, pairwise + per-type 分析）。检验 confusability 效应的跨模型 泛化性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_f1_count64\": 0.378,\n      \"baseline_vs_qwen3\": \"Δ=-3.6pp (Qwen3=0.414)\",\n      \"pairwise_qwen3_embed\": {\n        \"pearson_r\": 0.042,\n        \"pearson_p\": 0.068,\n        \"n_pairs\": 1953,\n        \"verdict\": \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n      },\n      \"pairwise_qwen3_embed_nonzero\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.078,\n        \"p\": 0.12,\n        \"verdict\": \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n      },\n      \"per_type_bcs_f1\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": -0.082,\n        \"p\": 0.538,\n        \"n_types\": 58,\n        \"partial_r_ctrl_logfreq\": -0.055,\n        \"partial_p\": 0.684,\n        \"verdict\": \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n      },\n      \"batch_f1_vs_bcs\": {\n        \"count_6\": {\n          \"r\": 0.108,\n          \"p\": 0.42\n        },\n        \"count_12\": {\n          \"r\": 0.185,\n          \"p\": 0.21\n        },\n        \"partial_pooled\": {\n          \"r\": 0.138,\n          \"p\": 0.16\n        }\n      },\n      \"confusion_rate_extreme\": {\n        \"count_6_high\": 0.025,\n        \"count_6_low\": 0.01,\n        \"ratio_6\": 2.5,\n        \"count_12_high\": 0.032,\n        \"count_12_low\": 0.015,\n        \"ratio_12\": 2.1\n      },\n      \"confusion_rate_random\": {\n        \"count_6_ratio\": 1.2,\n        \"count_12_ratio\": 1.15\n      },\n      \"cross_model_summary\": {\n        \"qwen3_pairwise_r\": 0.156,\n        \"llama_pairwise_r\": 0.042,\n        \"qwen3_extreme_ratio\": \"10-28x\",\n        \"llama_extreme_ratio\": \"2.1-2.5x\",\n        \"qwen3_per_type_rho\": -0.293,\n        \"llama_per_type_rho\": -0.082\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: Cross-Model Comparison (Few-NERD)\\n| Metric                    | Qwen3-32B    | LLaMA-3.3-70B | Ratio    |\\n|---------------------------|-------------|---------------|----------|\\n| Baseline F1 (count_64)    | 0.414       | 0.378         | 0.91x    |\\n| Pairwise r (Qwen3 embed)  | 0.156***    | 0.042 (ns)    | 0.27x    |\\n| Per-type ρ                | -0.293*     | -0.082 (ns)   | 0.28x    |\\n| Extreme confusion ratio   | 10-28x      | 2.1-2.5x      | 0.10x    |\\n| Random confusion ratio    | 1.7-2.4x    | 1.15-1.2x     | 0.50x    |\\n\",\n      \"Table: LLaMA Pairwise & Per-Type Statistics\\n| Analysis        | Statistic | Value  | p     | Verdict |\\n|-----------------|-----------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| Pairwise        | Pearson r | 0.042  | 0.068 | NS      |\\n| Pairwise NZ     | Spearman  | 0.078  | 0.120 | NS      |\\n| Per-type        | Spearman  | -0.082 | 0.538 | NS      |\\n| Per-type partial| Partial r | -0.055 | 0.684 | NS      |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"LLaMA 结果是 worst tier 中最关键的 negative result。cross_model_significant = 1 （仅 Qwen3），这意味着 confusability 效应可能是 Qwen3 特有的，而非 LLM IE 的 普遍现象。论文必须显著降级 Claim 1 的 generalizability：从 \\\"confusability independently predicts degradation in training-free LLM IE\\\" 改为 \\\"confusability sensitivity varies substantially across model families, with Qwen3 showing strong effects (r=0.156) and LLaMA showing weak/null effects (r=0.042)\\\"。在 worst tier 叙事中，这可 reframe 为解释力：\\\"prior conflicting findings about schema complexity may be partly explained by model-dependent confusability sensitivity\\\"——将缺陷转为贡献，但 reviewer 是否买账取决于写作。\\n\\n\\nLLaMA-3.3-70B 与 Qwen3-32B 在 confusability 敏感度上存在根本差异，原因可能是： (1) 模型规模差异——70B vs 32B，更大的模型有更大的 attention capacity，能更好地 处理 confusable types 的共现，因此 confusability 的 degradation 效应被缓解； (2) instruction tuning 差异——LLaMA-3.3 的 RLHF 训练可能更强调 precision 和 faithfulness，模型在不确定时倾向不输出（而非猜测相似 type），导致 type confusion error 本就少，confusability 信号弱；(3) internal representation 差异——LLaMA 的 embedding 空间对 Few-NERD types 的组织方式可能与 Qwen3 不同，Qwen3 embedding 中的 semantic proximity 模式不能直接迁移为 LLaMA 的 confusion 模式。\\npairwise r=0.042 (p=0.068) 在 α=0.05 下不显著但接近边界——这是最棘手的 结果：不能说完全无信号（p=0.068），但也不能声称显著。在 worst tier 叙事中， 这被 reframe 为 \\\"confusability effects are model-dependent, with effect size varying by 4x across model families (r=0.156 Qwen3 vs r=0.042 LLaMA)\\\"。confusion rate ratio 也大幅下降（2.5x vs Qwen3 的 27.5x），进一步说明 LLaMA 对 type confusion 更鲁棒。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\",\n    \"description\": \"Few-NERD 上的 SDGD-zero：Qwen3 embedding SCS + graph coloring (τ adaptive, k=1.0) 生成 confusability-minimizing batches，与 single-pass 对比。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"graph_stats\": {\n        \"threshold_tau\": 0.847,\n        \"n_edges\": 142,\n        \"edge_density\": 0.066,\n        \"chromatic_number\": 8,\n        \"avg_batch_size\": 8.25,\n        \"max_batch_size\": 12,\n        \"min_batch_size\": 4,\n        \"max_intra_batch_bcs\": 0.842\n      },\n      \"sdgd_zero\": {\n        \"f1\": 0.367,\n        \"precision\": 0.318,\n        \"recall\": 0.434,\n        \"pred_gold_ratio\": 1.36\n      },\n      \"single_pass\": {\n        \"f1\": 0.414,\n        \"precision\": 0.648,\n        \"recall\": 0.304\n      },\n      \"delta_f1_vs_single_pass\": -4.7,\n      \"delta_precision\": -33.0,\n      \"delta_recall\": 13.0,\n      \"per_batch_f1_range\": [\n        0.28,\n        0.42\n      ],\n      \"per_batch_recall_range\": [\n        0.35,\n        0.52\n      ],\n      \"per_batch_precision_range\": [\n        0.22,\n        0.38\n      ],\n      \"merge_stats\": {\n        \"total_predictions\": 4850,\n        \"unique_predictions_after_dedup\": 4120,\n        \"cross_batch_span_overlap\": 0.08,\n        \"predictions_per_sample_avg\": 8.2,\n        \"gold_per_sample_avg\": 5.9\n      },\n      \"api_calls\": \"8x single-pass (8000 vs 1000 for 1000 samples)\",\n      \"wall_clock_multiplier\": 6.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass (Few-NERD, 66 types)\\n| Method      | F1    | Precision | Recall | Pred/Gold | API Calls |\\n|-------------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------|-----------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.648     | 0.304  | 0.47      | 1x        |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | 0.318     | 0.434  | 1.36      | 8x        |\\n| Δ           | -4.7pp| -33.0pp   | +13.0pp| +0.89     | +7x       |\\n\",\n      \"Table: SDGD-zero Per-Batch Breakdown (top 4 batches)\\n| Batch | Types | Avg BCS | F1    | Recall | Precision |\\n|-------|-------|---------|-------|--------|-----------|\\n| 0     | 12    | 0.812   | 0.42  | 0.48   | 0.38      |\\n| 1     | 10    | 0.795   | 0.38  | 0.45   | 0.33      |\\n| 2     | 9     | 0.780   | 0.35  | 0.42   | 0.30      |\\n| 3     | 8     | 0.763   | 0.32  | 0.40   | 0.27      |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SDGD-zero 的失败是 worst tier 的核心 negative result。直接否定 Claim 3。 failure mode 清晰且可解释：separating confusable types 剥夺了模型的 comparative disambiguation 能力。这是一个 informative negative result——它揭示了 LLM IE 中 type co-presence 的 dual role：(1) 增加 confusability（hypothesis 的前提）， (2) 提供 disambiguation context（SDGD 未预见的副作用）。在 worst tier 叙事中， 这个发现可以作为论文的一个 insight：\\\"confusability is a two-edged sword — the same type co-presence that causes confusion also enables disambiguation\\\"， 解释为什么简单的 separation strategy 不 work。但这最多放在 Discussion section， 不能作为 core contribution。\\n\\n\\nSDGD-zero 失败的核心机制是 \\\"disambiguation context loss\\\"。当 confusable types 被分到不同 batch 时，每个 batch 中的模型只看到 pair 的一端。例如 person-other 在 batch A，person-politician 在 batch B。处理含政治人物的句子时：\\n- Batch A（有 person-other，无 person-politician）：模型将政治人物标为\\n  person-other（因为这是最接近的可用 type）→ FP for person-other\\n- Batch B（有 person-politician，无 person-other）：模型将普通人标为\\n  person-politician（同理）→ FP for person-politician\\n\\nmerge 后，同一实体可能被两个 batch 分别标为不同 type（cross-batch span overlap 8%），评估时只有一个是 TP，另一个是 FP。更严重的是，每个 batch 只有 ~8 types， 模型倾向过度提取（pred/gold=1.36 vs single-pass 的 0.47），precision 从 0.648 暴跌到 0.318。recall 确实从 0.304 提升到 0.434（smaller batch → 更多 attention 给每个 type），但 precision 损失远大于 recall 增益。\\nF1 = 0.367 比 single-pass 的 0.414 低 4.7pp。SDGD 的前提假设（separating confusable types reduces confusion）是错误的——对 LLM 来说，看到 confusable types 的完整集合反而帮助 disambiguation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\",\n    \"description\": \"MAVEN（168 event types）上的 SDGD-zero。用 adaptive threshold (k=1.0) 生成 confusability-minimizing batches。跨任务（NER→ED）验证 SDGD。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"graph_stats\": {\n        \"embedding\": \"qwen3\",\n        \"scs_mean\": 0.216,\n        \"scs_std\": 0.103,\n        \"threshold_tau\": 0.319,\n        \"n_edges\": 1850,\n        \"edge_density\": 0.132,\n        \"chromatic_number\": 15,\n        \"avg_batch_size\": 11.2,\n        \"min_batch_size\": 5,\n        \"max_batch_size\": 18\n      },\n      \"sdgd_zero\": {\n        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.168,\n        \"exact_f1\": 0.012,\n        \"relaxed_recall\": 0.13,\n        \"relaxed_precision\": 0.238\n      },\n      \"single_pass\": {\n        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.241,\n        \"exact_f1\": 0.018\n      },\n      \"delta_relaxed_f1\": -7.3,\n      \"api_calls\": \"15x single-pass\",\n      \"wall_clock_multiplier\": 12.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass (MAVEN, 168 types)\\n| Method      | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\\n|-------------|-----------|----------|-----------|------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.241     | 0.018    | 1x        | 1x         |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | 0.012    | 15x       | 12.8x      |\\n| Δ           | -7.3pp    | -0.6pp   | +14x      | +11.8x     |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN SDGD-zero 是最差的结果之一。15x API cost 换来 -7.3pp 性能下降。 与 Few-NERD 的 SDGD 失败共同构成 Claim 3 的致命反证：SDGD 在两个任务上 都差于 single-pass，且效果 consistent（方向一致、机制相同）。在 worst tier 叙事中，SDGD 相关实验（exp-008, 009, 010, 011, 013, 014）全部降级为 appendix 中的 negative result case study，正文仅用 1-2 段文字总结 \\\"we also explored confusability-minimizing decomposition, which failed because...\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMAVEN 上 SDGD-zero 失败更严重（Δ=-7.3pp vs Few-NERD 的 -4.7pp），原因： (1) MAVEN count curve 是上升的——更多 types 帮助模型理解 event ontology， decomposition 直接损害这个优势；(2) adaptive τ=0.319（因 MAVEN Qwen3 SCS 分布集中在低值区间），graph 中 edge density=13.2%，coloring 产生 15 个 batch， 每个约 11 types——这比 single-pass 的 168 types 少了 93%的 type 上下文； (3) 15 个 batch 意味着 15x API 调用，wall-clock 12.8x 但性能反而更差—— cost-quality 全面恶化；(4) MAVEN event trigger 是 verb/nominalization，多个 event type 共享同一 trigger word（如 \\\"attack\\\" 可以是 Attack 也可以是 Conflict）， 模型需要看到完整 event taxonomy 才能正确 assign type。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\",\n    \"description\": \"Few-NERD 上的 SDGD-cal：用 5-10 calibration examples 构建 empirical confusion matrix，替代 embedding SCS。与 SDGD-zero 和 single-pass 对比。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"calibration_stats\": {\n        \"n_calibration_samples\": 8,\n        \"calibration_api_calls\": 8,\n        \"empirical_confusion_pairs_nonzero\": 85,\n        \"spearman_vs_embedding_scs\": 0.125,\n        \"p_vs_embedding_scs\": 0.031\n      },\n      \"graph_stats\": {\n        \"threshold_tau\": \"adaptive on empirical confusion\",\n        \"n_edges\": 62,\n        \"chromatic_number\": 7,\n        \"avg_batch_size\": 9.4\n      },\n      \"sdgd_cal\": {\n        \"f1\": 0.381,\n        \"precision\": 0.342,\n        \"recall\": 0.43,\n        \"pred_gold_ratio\": 1.26\n      },\n      \"comparison\": {\n        \"vs_single_pass_delta\": -3.3,\n        \"vs_sdgd_zero_delta\": 1.4,\n        \"vs_random_delta\": 0.7,\n        \"vs_random_p\": 0.58\n      },\n      \"single_pass_f1\": 0.414,\n      \"sdgd_zero_f1\": 0.367,\n      \"random_f1\": 0.374\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (Few-NERD)\\n| Method      | F1    | Δ vs SP | Precision | Recall | API Overhead   |\\n|-------------|-------|---------|-----------|--------|----------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.414 | —       | 0.648     | 0.304  | 1x             |\\n| Random (k=8)| 0.374 | -4.0    | 0.335     | 0.425  | 8x             |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | -4.7    | 0.318     | 0.434  | 8x             |\\n| SDGD-cal    | 0.381 | -3.3    | 0.342     | 0.430  | 7x + 8 calib   |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SDGD-cal 是 SDGD 方法线的 \\\"best effort\\\"——用 ground truth confusion 替代 proxy。 即使如此仍低于 single-pass 3.3pp。这最终否定了 confusability-minimizing decomposition 的整体方法路线：问题不在 confusion matrix 的质量，而在于 decomposition 本身损害了 LLM 的 disambiguation context。在 worst tier 叙事中， SDGD-cal 的 marginal improvement over SDGD-zero 可作为 exp-015（SCS validation） 的间接证据：embedding proxy 与 empirical confusion 仅弱相关（ρ=0.125），但这 不是失败的主因——即使 perfect confusion matrix 也不能拯救 decomposition strategy。\\n\\n\\nSDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 好（+1.4pp），因为 empirical confusion matrix 比 embedding SCS 更准确地反映实际 model confusion：(1) 非零 confusion pair 只有 85 对（vs embedding SCS 的 142 条 edge），graph 更稀疏 → 7 个 batch（vs 8 个），每个 batch 更大 → 更多 type 上下文；(2) calibration 捕捉到一些 embedding SCS 预测不 到的 confusion pattern（如语义不近但 surface form 相似的 type pair）。但 SDGD-cal 仍低于 single-pass 3.3pp，因为 decomposition 的核心问题（disambiguation context loss）不因 confusion matrix 质量改善而消失。与 random batching 的差异仅 +0.7pp (p=0.58)，不显著——confusability-aware grouping 即使用了 empirical data 也没有 显著优势。calibration 的额外 cost（8 次 API 调用）换来的 improvement 微乎其微。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\",\n    \"description\": \"MAVEN（168 types）上的 SDGD-cal：empirical confusion matrix + graph coloring。 Full comparison table。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"calibration_stats\": {\n        \"n_calibration_samples\": 10,\n        \"empirical_confusion_pairs_nonzero\": 210\n      },\n      \"graph_stats\": {\n        \"chromatic_number\": 12,\n        \"avg_batch_size\": 14.0\n      },\n      \"sdgd_cal\": {\n        \"relaxed_f1\": 0.188,\n        \"exact_f1\": 0.014\n      },\n      \"comparison\": {\n        \"vs_single_pass_delta\": -5.3,\n        \"vs_sdgd_zero_delta\": 2.0,\n        \"vs_random_delta\": 0.8,\n        \"vs_random_p\": 0.62\n      },\n      \"single_pass_relaxed_f1\": 0.241,\n      \"sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1\": 0.168,\n      \"random_relaxed_f1\": 0.18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: Full Comparison (MAVEN, 168 types, relaxed matching)\\n| Method      | Relaxed F1 | Δ vs SP | API Calls      |\\n|-------------|-----------|---------|----------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.241     | —       | 1x             |\\n| Random (k=12)| 0.180    | -6.1    | 12x            |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | -7.3    | 15x            |\\n| SDGD-cal    | 0.188     | -5.3    | 12x + 10 calib |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MAVEN SDGD-cal 确认 decomposition 在 event detection 上全面失败。所有方法 均差于 single-pass，且 MAVEN 的差距（5-7pp）比 Few-NERD（3-5pp）更大。 这强化了 worst tier 的核心结论：decomposition 不是通用 solution，type co-presence 在很多场景中是 feature 而非 bug。\\n\\n\\n与 Few-NERD 相同模式：SDGD-cal 好于 SDGD-zero（+2.0pp）但仍远差于 single-pass （-5.3pp）。MAVEN 的 empirical confusion matrix 更密（210 nonzero pairs vs Few-NERD 的 85），因为 168 types 中很多 event type 确实会互相 confuse（尤其是 同一 FrameNet frame 下的 sibling types）。但 calibration 帮助有限——核心问题 仍然是 MAVEN 的性能与 type count 正相关，decomposition 损害性能。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Random Batching Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"与 SDGD-zero 相同 batch 数量 k，随机分组。隔离 confusability-aware grouping 的价值（排除 batch count reduction 的贡献）。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"fewnerd\": {\n        \"random_f1\": 0.374,\n        \"sdgd_zero_f1\": 0.367,\n        \"delta_sdgd_vs_random\": -0.7,\n        \"paired_t_p\": 0.68,\n        \"n_random_seeds\": 10,\n        \"random_f1_std\": 0.018,\n        \"random_f1_range\": [\n          0.348,\n          0.402\n        ],\n        \"single_pass_f1\": 0.414\n      },\n      \"maven\": {\n        \"random_relaxed_f1\": 0.18,\n        \"sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1\": 0.168,\n        \"delta_sdgd_vs_random\": -1.2,\n        \"paired_t_p\": 0.42,\n        \"n_random_seeds\": 5\n      },\n      \"interpretation\": {\n        \"sdgd_vs_random_significant\": false,\n        \"confusability_aware_grouping_benefit\": null\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: Random vs SDGD-zero (Few-NERD, k=8)\\n| Method     | Mean F1 | Std   | Range         | vs Single-Pass |\\n|------------|---------|-------|---------------|----------------|\\n| Random×10  | 0.374   | 0.018 | [0.348,0.402] | -4.0pp         |\\n| SDGD-zero  | 0.367   | —     | —             | -4.7pp         |\\n| Δ (SDGD-Random) | -0.7pp | — | —           | p=0.68 (NS)    |\\n\",\n      \"Table: Random vs SDGD-zero (MAVEN, k=15/12)\\n| Method     | Relaxed F1 | vs Single-Pass |\\n|------------|-----------|----------------|\\n| Random×5   | 0.180     | -6.1pp         |\\n| SDGD-zero  | 0.168     | -7.3pp         |\\n| Δ          | -1.2pp    | p=0.42 (NS)    |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Random batching ablation 是 Claim 3 的 definitive kill shot。SDGD 不显著优于 random→confusability-aware grouping 无价值。combined with SDGD < single-pass→ decomposition 本身有害。Claim 3 完全不成立。在 worst tier 叙事中，这个实验 的 negative result 本身有教育意义：it demonstrates that the intuitive principle \\\"separate confusable types\\\" is wrong for LLM IE，因为 LLMs 使用 type co-presence 做 comparative reasoning。\\n\\n\\nRandom batching 在 10 个 random seeds 上平均 F1=0.374（std=0.018），而 SDGD-zero F1=0.367。SDGD 比 random 差 0.7pp（p=0.68），差异不显著。实际上 SDGD 可能略 差于 random，因为 SDGD 刻意将 confusable types 分开——这意味着每个 batch 内的 types 都是 semantically distant 的，模型缺乏同一 semantic cluster 的 types 作为 disambiguation anchor。Random batching 偶尔会把 confusable types 放在一起 （概率约 1/k），这些 batch 的 disambiguation 更好，平均下来 random 反而略优。\\n在 MAVEN 上同样：random F1=0.180 vs SDGD F1=0.168（Δ=-1.2pp, p=0.42）。 SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 不仅无益，可能有害。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-Type Splitting (UniNER-style) Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"1 type per batch（k=66/168）。Decomposition 的上界。揭示 latency-quality tradeoff。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"fewnerd\": {\n        \"per_type_f1\": 0.33,\n        \"per_type_precision\": 0.225,\n        \"per_type_recall\": 0.62,\n        \"api_calls\": \"66x single-pass\",\n        \"wall_clock_multiplier\": 48.0\n      },\n      \"maven\": {\n        \"per_type_relaxed_f1\": 0.108,\n        \"api_calls\": \"168x single-pass\",\n        \"wall_clock_multiplier\": 135.0\n      },\n      \"comparison_fewnerd\": {\n        \"single_pass\": 0.414,\n        \"sdgd_zero\": 0.367,\n        \"random\": 0.374,\n        \"per_type\": 0.33\n      },\n      \"ordering\": \"single-pass > random ≈ SDGD-zero > per-type\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: Full Method Comparison (Few-NERD)\\n| Method      | F1    | Precision | Recall | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\\n|-------------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------|------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.648     | 0.304  | 1x        | 1x         |\\n| SDGD-cal    | 0.381 | 0.342     | 0.430  | 7x        | 5.5x       |\\n| Random (k=8)| 0.374 | 0.335     | 0.425  | 8x        | 6.5x       |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | 0.318     | 0.434  | 8x        | 6.5x       |\\n| Per-type    | 0.330 | 0.225     | 0.620  | 66x       | 48x        |\\n\",\n      \"Table: Full Method Comparison (MAVEN, relaxed)\\n| Method      | Relaxed F1 | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\\n|-------------|-----------|-----------|------------|\\n| Single-pass | 0.241     | 1x        | 1x         |\\n| SDGD-cal    | 0.188     | 12x       | 10x        |\\n| Random      | 0.180     | 12x       | 10x        |\\n| SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | 15x       | 12.8x      |\\n| Per-type    | 0.108     | 168x      | 135x       |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Per-type ablation 完成了 decomposition failure 的完整图景。方法排序 single-pass > random ≈ SDGD > per-type 说明：(1) decomposition granularity 与 F1 反相关；(2) type co-presence 是 net positive（disambiguation > confusion）； (3) SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 不提供额外价值（≈ random）。 在 worst tier 叙事中，这个结果可 reframe 为 empirical finding：\\\"LLM IE benefits from full schema visibility; type co-presence enables comparative reasoning that outweighs confusability-induced errors\\\"——这本身是一个有价值 的 insight，但不是 method contribution。\\n\\n\\nPer-type splitting 是 decomposition 的极端形式：每个 batch 只有 1 个 type。 这完全消除 type confusion（BCS=0），但也完全消除 disambiguation context。\\nFew-NERD 结果（F1=0.330）几乎等于 exp003a count_1 的 F1=0.323——符合预期， 因为 per-type extraction 本质就是 count=1。precision 极低（0.225）因为模型 只知道一个 type，会把任何像样的 span 都标为该 type（massive over-extraction）。 recall 最高（0.620）因为模型 aggressively 搜索这个 type 的所有 instance。\\nMAVEN 更惨（relaxed F1=0.108），因为 MAVEN 的 count_1 relaxed_F1 就只有 0.098。 168x API 调用使 wall-clock time 完全不可接受。\\n排序 single-pass > random ≈ SDGD > per-type 证明：decomposition granularity 与性能成反比。batch 越大越好（更多 type context），单pass 最优。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Embedding SCS vs Empirical Confusion Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"计算 embedding SCS（Qwen3 / MiniLM）与 empirical confusion matrix 之间的 rank correlation。验证 embedding proxy 对实际 model confusion 的预测力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen3_scs_vs_empirical\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.125,\n        \"p\": 0.031,\n        \"kendall_tau\": 0.092,\n        \"p_kendall\": 0.044,\n        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 85\n      },\n      \"minilm_scs_vs_empirical\": {\n        \"spearman_rho\": 0.098,\n        \"p\": 0.082,\n        \"kendall_tau\": 0.071,\n        \"p_kendall\": 0.115,\n        \"n_pairs_with_confusion\": 85\n      },\n      \"top_confused_pair_scs_rank\": {\n        \"person_other_politician\": {\n          \"scs_rank\": 3,\n          \"confusion_rank\": 1\n        },\n        \"building_other_library\": {\n          \"scs_rank\": 45,\n          \"confusion_rank\": 8,\n          \"comment\": \"high confusion, low SCS — embedding 未捕捉的 confusion pattern\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"scs_false_positive_rate\": 0.42,\n      \"scs_false_negative_rate\": 0.35\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation\\n| Embedding | Spearman ρ | p     | Kendall τ | p     |\\n|-----------|-----------|-------|-----------|-------|\\n| Qwen3     | 0.125     | 0.031 | 0.092     | 0.044 |\\n| MiniLM    | 0.098     | 0.082 | 0.071     | 0.115 |\\n\",\n      \"Table: SCS Proxy Error Analysis\\n| Metric              | Qwen3 | MiniLM |\\n|---------------------|-------|--------|\\n| False Positive Rate | 0.42  | 0.48   |\\n| False Negative Rate | 0.35  | 0.40   |\\n| Top-1 Match         | Yes   | No     |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SCS validation 结果解释了 SDGD 失败的一个次要原因（proxy 质量差），但不是主因 （主因是 decomposition 本身有害）。ρ=0.125 说明 embedding SCS 只能解释 ~1.6% 的 confusion variance——作为 graph 构建的基础远远不够。即使用 empirical confusion (exp-010 SDGD-cal) 也只比 random 好 0.7pp（不显著），所以 proxy 质量不是瓶颈。 在 worst tier 叙事中，SCS validation 作为 methodological finding 报告： \\\"embedding-based confusability proxies have limited predictive power for actual model confusion patterns, suggesting that confusability is mediated by factors beyond semantic similarity\\\"——这对未来工作有指导价值。\\n\\n\\nEmbedding SCS 与 empirical confusion 仅弱相关（ρ=0.125），原因：(1) embedding similarity 反映 semantic proximity，但 model confusion 还受 surface form similarity、type definition wording、in-context position 等因素影响——这些因素 与 embedding space 正交；(2) SCS 是对称的（sim(A,B)=sim(B,A)），但实际 confusion 是非对称的（person-other → person-politician 的概率可能远高于反向）；(3) 42% 的 false positive rate 意味着 SCS 预测为 confusable 的 type pair 中近一半实际 不被 confuse——这些 false alarm 导致 SDGD-zero 过度分离 types，graph 变密， batch 数量过多。\\nMiniLM SCS 更差（ρ=0.098, p=0.082），因为 MiniLM 是 general-purpose sentence embedding，不 align 到 Qwen3 的 internal representation。这解释了为什么 extraction model alignment 对 per-type signal 很重要（exp-002 中 Qwen3 per-type ρ=-0.293 vs MiniLM ρ≈0）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Experiment Summary (for paper narrative)\",\n    \"description\": \"综合所有实验的 worst tier 结果，构建论文核心 tables 和 narrative。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"claim1_pairwise_matrix\": {\n        \"qwen3_fewnerd\": \"r=0.156*** ✓\",\n        \"qwen3_maven\": \"r=-0.009 (ns) ✗\",\n        \"qwen3_fewrel\": \"pending\",\n        \"minilm_fewnerd\": \"not tested\",\n        \"minilm_maven\": \"r=0.115*** ✓\",\n        \"minilm_fewrel\": \"Δ=21-50pp ✓ (pilot)\",\n        \"llama_fewnerd\": \"r=0.042 (ns) ✗\",\n        \"significant_cells\": 3,\n        \"total_cells\": 7,\n        \"verdict\": \"partial — 3/7 significant, no single embedding/model universally works\"\n      },\n      \"claim2_evidence\": {\n        \"count_recall_monotonic\": true,\n        \"bcs_type_substitution_ratio_extreme\": \"4.8x\",\n        \"bcs_type_substitution_ratio_random\": \"1.5x\",\n        \"interaction_significant\": false,\n        \"error_taxonomy_dominant_mode\": \"spurious extraction (45%), not type confusion (18%)\",\n        \"verdict\": \"directional — channels exist but confusability channel is weak relative to other error sources\"\n      },\n      \"claim3_evidence\": {\n        \"sdgd_zero_fewnerd\": \"F1=0.367, Δ=-4.7pp vs SP\",\n        \"sdgd_zero_maven\": \"relF1=0.168, Δ=-7.3pp vs SP\",\n        \"sdgd_cal_fewnerd\": \"F1=0.381, Δ=-3.3pp vs SP\",\n        \"sdgd_cal_maven\": \"relF1=0.188, Δ=-5.3pp vs SP\",\n        \"sdgd_vs_random_significant\": false,\n        \"per_type_worst\": true,\n        \"verdict\": \"FAILED — all decomposition methods inferior to single-pass\"\n      },\n      \"recommended_paper_structure\": [\n        \"1. Introduction: 'What makes schemas complex for LLMs?'\",\n        \"2. Related Work: decomposition approaches + empirical studies\",\n        \"3. Experimental Setup: 3 tasks, 2 models, 2 embeddings\",\n        \"4. Finding 1: Pairwise confusability predicts type confusion (model-dependent)\",\n        \"5. Finding 2: Count and confusability act through distinguishable channels\",\n        \"6. Finding 3: Per-type aggregation introduces centrality confound\",\n        \"7. Finding 4: Confusability-minimizing decomposition fails (negative result)\",\n        \"8. Discussion: implications for future work\",\n        \"9. Conclusion\"\n      ],\n      \"recommended_venue\": \"EMNLP 2026 Findings (realistic), Main (stretch)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: Pairwise SCS-Confusion Signal (Cross-Task × Cross-Model × Cross-Embedding)\\n| Model  | Embedding | Few-NERD (NER) | MAVEN (ED) | FewRel (RE) |\\n|--------|-----------|----------------|------------|-------------|\\n| Qwen3  | Qwen3     | r=0.156***     | r=-0.009   | —           |\\n| Qwen3  | MiniLM    | —              | r=0.115*** | Δ=21-50pp*  |\\n| LLaMA  | Qwen3     | r=0.042        | —          | —           |\\n*** p<0.001, * pilot only\\n\",\n      \"Table: SDGD Full Comparison (worst tier)\\n| Method       | Few-NERD F1 | Δ vs SP | MAVEN relF1 | Δ vs SP |\\n|-------------|-------------|---------|-------------|---------|\\n| Single-pass  | 0.414       | —       | 0.241       | —       |\\n| SDGD-cal     | 0.381       | -3.3    | 0.188       | -5.3    |\\n| Random (=k)  | 0.374       | -4.0    | 0.180       | -6.1    |\\n| SDGD-zero    | 0.367       | -4.7    | 0.168       | -7.3    |\\n| Per-type     | 0.330       | -8.4    | 0.108       | -13.3   |\\n\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 论文的核心卖点不是 positive findings 而是 systematic methodology 和 honest reporting。三个 takeaway：(1) confusability 信号存在但 model/embedding-dependent——未来工作不能假设 universal confusability measure； (2) per-type 聚合有 centrality confound——未来工作应使用 pairwise 分析； (3) confusability-minimizing decomposition 失败——LLM 需要 type co-presence 做 comparative reasoning，简单分离策略适得其反。这些 negative-but-informative results 加上 controlled experimental design 可以支撑一篇 Findings paper。\\n\\nWorst tier 总体图景：论文有两个可靠发现（pairwise confusability signal on Qwen3×FewNERD + MiniLM×MAVEN；centrality confound on MAVEN）和一系列 informative negative results（LLaMA 无信号、SDGD 全面失败、interaction 不显著）。叙事必须 从 \\\"we discover and exploit confusability\\\" 彻底转为 \\\"we systematically investigate schema complexity, finding that confusability effects are real but model-dependent, and that the intuitive decomposition strategy fails because LLMs need type co-presence for disambiguation\\\"。这种 \\\"honest empirical study with negative results\\\" 的论文在 EMNLP Findings 有先例（如 \\\"Do Prompt-Based Models Really Understand the Meaning of Their Prompts?\\\" ACL 2022），但需要极强的写作功力 和清晰的 takeaway。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":634,"startLine":1,"totalLines":634}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015hLztxoUbubHXgfkxXjS84","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — schema-dag-extraction\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 cycle)\n5\t- Commitment deadline: August 2, 2026\n6\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings (same ARR cycle, commitment August 26)\n7\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (10 days from today)\n8\t\n9\t## Core Claims (3 conditions) — Revised per D012\n10\t\n11\t1. **Confusability Independence**: Type confusability independently predicts extraction quality degradation in training-free LLM IE, beyond what type count alone explains. The signal is strongest and most robust at the **type-pair level** (pairwise SCS → confusion), validated across NER (Few-NERD), RE (FewRel), and ED (MAVEN with MiniLM). Per-type aggregation (mean BCS) introduces a centrality confound in semantically homogeneous schemas. Evidence required: (a) significant pairwise SCS-confusion correlation on >=2 datasets, (b) extreme-batch accuracy gap on FewRel, (c) >=2 models.\n12\t\n13\t2. **Multi-Channel Degradation**: Count and confusability degrade extraction through orthogonal channels -- count causes entity omission (recall decline), while confusability causes type confusion errors (correct spans labeled with wrong types). Evidence required: error taxonomy showing differential error types per channel, monotonic trends in separate metrics.\n14\t\n15\t3. **SDGD Effectiveness**: Confusability-aware schema decomposition (SDGD) -- partitioning types into low-confusability batches via graph coloring on the pairwise-similarity-thresholded graph -- yields significant F1 gains over single-pass and heuristic decomposition on complex schemas (>=30 types). SDGD directly leverages pairwise confusability (validated signal), avoiding per-type aggregation confounds. Evidence required: SDGD > single-pass, SDGD > random batching (same k), SDGD >= per-type splitting (with lower latency).\n16\t\n17\t## Story Spine — Revised per D012\n18\t\n19\t- **Problem**: Training-free LLM IE degrades severely on complex schemas (20-60 F1 gap vs supervised). All existing decomposition approaches operate on unvalidated assumptions about WHAT makes schemas complex for LLMs.\n20\t\n21\t- **Existing approaches & their gaps**: UniNER splits per-type (gains 3.3 F1 but loses cross-type context, no criterion for when to split). LLM-PEE uses similarity as implicit confusability proxy (never validated empirically). No prior work isolates confusability from count, or characterizes when aggregated confusability measures lose signal.\n22\t\n23\t- **Our framing**: We conduct the first controlled empirical study isolating type confusability from type count in training-free LLM IE across three tasks (NER, RE, ED). We discover: (1) a multi-channel degradation model (count→recall, confusability→type confusion), (2) pairwise type confusability is a robust cross-task signal, (3) per-type aggregation of confusability is confounded by type centrality in homogeneous schemas. We operationalize pairwise confusability into SDGD, a principled framework for confusability-minimizing schema decomposition.\n24\t\n25\t- **Three-task validation**:\n26\t  - NER (Few-NERD, 66 types, cross-domain): Pairwise r=0.156 (p<1e-11), per-type ρ=-0.293 (p=0.02), 10-28x confusion ratio\n27\t  - RE (FewRel, 80 relations, cross-domain): Extreme-batch accuracy gap Δ=21-50pp\n28\t  - ED (MAVEN, 168 event types, same-domain): Pairwise MiniLM r=0.120 (p≈0); per-type positive (centrality confound case study)\n29\t\n30\t- **Headline result template**: \"Pairwise type confusability independently predicts extraction degradation across NER, RE, and ED tasks (r=0.12-0.16, p<1e-6), with 10-28x more type confusion errors in high-confusability batches. On semantically homogeneous schemas, per-type aggregation obscures the signal through centrality confounding, but pairwise confusability remains valid. SDGD-zero, operating on pairwise similarity, improves F1 by X points over single-pass on Few-NERD.\"\n31\t\n32\t## Core Insight — Multi-Channel Degradation + Pairwise Robustness\n33\t\n34\tSchema-induced degradation in LLM IE is not a single phenomenon but a multi-channel process:\n35\t- **Channel 1 (Count -> Recall)**: More types in the prompt → attention dilution → entities missed. Monotonic, near-linear. Addressable by reducing batch size.\n36\t- **Channel 2 (Confusability -> Type Confusion)**: Semantically similar co-present types → interference during type assignment → correct entities labeled with wrong types. Addressable by separating confusable types into different batches.\n37\t\n38\tThese channels are orthogonal and independently addressable.\n39\t\n40\t**Pairwise vs Aggregated Confusability**:\n41\t- **Pairwise confusability** (SCS between type pairs) is robust across all tasks and schema types. Validated on Few-NERD (Qwen3, r=0.156) and MAVEN (MiniLM, r=0.120).\n42\t- **Per-type aggregation** (mean BCS = average pairwise similarity to all other types) introduces a centrality confound: in semantically homogeneous schemas (MAVEN), types with many semantic neighbors are central, well-represented types that LLMs extract well → positive correlation (high mean BCS → high F1), masking the pairwise confusability signal.\n43\t- **SDGD operates at pairwise level**, directly using the validated signal to construct the confusability graph for decomposition. It avoids the aggregation confound entirely.\n44\t\n45\t## Evidence Hierarchy (D012)\n46\t\n47\t### Tier 1: PRIMARY — Pairwise SCS → Confusion\n48\t\n49\tThe cleanest evidence. Directly measures: are semantically similar type pairs more often confused?\n50\t\n51\t**Few-NERD (NER)** — Qwen3 embeddings:\n52\t- Pearson r=0.156 (p=4.6e-12, n=1953 type pairs)\n53\t- Nonzero-only Spearman ρ=0.254 (p=1.1e-6)\n54\t- Top confused pairs are all high-BCS semantic neighbors (person-other ↔ person-politician, BCS=0.934)\n55\t- Immune to type frequency confound (operates at type-pair level)\n56\t\n57\t**MAVEN (ED)** — MiniLM embeddings:\n58\t- Pearson r=+0.120 (p≈0, n=11026 type pairs)\n59\t- Nonzero-only Spearman ρ=+0.191 (p<0.001)\n60\t- Cross-task replication on same-domain schema\n61\t- Note: Qwen3 pairwise not significant on MAVEN (r=-0.007, p=0.41) — embedding choice matters for pairwise signal in homogeneous schemas\n62\t\n63\t### Tier 2: STRONG SECONDARY — FewRel Extreme-Batch Comparison\n64\t\n65\tLarge effect size, cross-task (RE), intuitive demonstration:\n66\t- count_4: low-BCS 91.7% vs high-BCS 70.8% (Δ=-20.9pp)\n67\t- count_8: low-BCS 100% vs high-BCS 50.0% (Δ=-50.0pp)\n68\t- count_16: low-BCS 91.7% vs high-BCS 43.1% (Δ=-48.6pp)\n69\t- Effect increases with count — consistent with multi-channel model\n70\t- MiniLM embeddings; pending: Qwen3 formal study\n71\t\n72\t### Tier 3: SUPPORTING — Few-NERD Per-type Analysis\n73\t\n74\tBridges pairwise and batch-level, demonstrates per-type signal in cross-domain schema:\n75\t- Spearman ρ=-0.293 (p=0.020, n=63 types, freq≥5) — Qwen3 embeddings\n76\t- Partial r=-0.200 (p=0.116) controlling for log-frequency\n77\t- Quartile comparison: high-BCS types F1=0.228 vs low-BCS F1=0.310 (Δ=-8.2pp)\n78\t- BCS-frequency uncorrelated at type level (r=0.042, p=0.74)\n79\t- MiniLM per-type: ρ≈0 (p=0.97) — extraction model alignment required for per-type signal\n80\t\n81\t### Tier 4: DISCUSSION — MAVEN Per-type Centrality Confound\n82\t\n83\tMethodological case study on when aggregated confusability measures fail:\n84\t- Qwen3 per-type: ρ=+0.189 (p=0.021) — OPPOSITE direction\n85\t- MiniLM per-type: ρ=+0.208 (p=0.011) — ALSO positive, ruling out embedding compression as sole explanation\n86\t- Both embeddings agree: positive direction on MAVEN is an intrinsic property of the type structure\n87\t- Explanation: in homogeneous schemas, mean BCS conflates confusability with type centrality (types with many semantic neighbors → common/central types → higher F1)\n88\t- This is stronger than \"domain boundary\" — it identifies the specific mechanism (aggregation confound) rather than just the boundary condition\n89\t\n90\t### Tier 5: MECHANISTIC — Error Taxonomy\n91\t\n92\tConfusion rate differential demonstrates the mechanism:\n93\t- Extreme batches: high-BCS 10-28x more type confusion errors vs low-BCS\n94\t- Random batches: 1.7-2.4x ratio (still significant, smaller effect)\n95\t- Type confusion errors increase with count AND with confusability (additive)\n96\t\n97\t## Embedding Ablation (D010)\n98\t\n99\t2×3 matrix: {Qwen3, MiniLM} × {Few-NERD, FewRel, MAVEN}\n100\t\n101\t### Per-type (Layer 2)\n102\t| | Few-NERD | FewRel | MAVEN |\n103\t|---|---|---|---|\n104\t| Qwen3 | ρ=-0.293 ✓ | pending | ρ=+0.189 ✗ |\n105\t| MiniLM | ρ≈0 ✗ | Δ=21-50pp ✓ | ρ=+0.208 ✗ |\n106\t\n107\t### Pairwise (Layer 1)\n108\t| | Few-NERD | MAVEN |\n109\t|---|---|---|\n110\t| Qwen3 | r=0.156 ✓ | r=-0.007 ✗ |\n111\t| MiniLM | — | r=+0.120 ✓ |\n112\t\n113\t**Interpretation**: No single embedding dominates. Extraction-model embeddings (Qwen3) capture per-type confusability in cross-domain schemas. Generic embeddings (MiniLM) capture pairwise confusability in same-domain schemas. SDGD should use task-appropriate embeddings; SDGD-cal (empirical confusion) bypasses embedding choice entirely.\n114\t\n115\t## Venue Fit Risks\n116\t\n117\t- **\"Just an empirical study\"**: Mitigated by SDGD as direct operationalization. Controlled experimental design parallels \"Lost in the Middle\" (TACL 2024).\n118\t- **Training-free IE relevance**: Cite deployment scenarios — clinical, regulatory, multilingual.\n119\t- **Multi-model generalizability**: Qwen3-32B primary + LLaMA-3.3-70B (exp-012).\n120\t- **MAVEN doesn't support hypothesis?**: Pairwise MiniLM does support it. Per-type centrality confound is methodological contribution, not failure.\n121\t- **Embedding sensitivity**: 2×3 ablation matrix is itself a contribution — characterizes when which proxy works.\n122\t\n123\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n124\t\n125\t| Concern | Response Strategy | Experiment |\n126\t|---------|------------------|------------|\n127\t| Only one model | LLaMA-3.3-70B replication | exp-012 |\n128\t| Cross-task replication | Pairwise: Few-NERD ✓ + MAVEN MiniLM ✓. Batch: FewRel ✓. Three tasks. | exp-002, exp-004, fewrel |\n129\t| No practical method | SDGD framework (-zero, -cal) | exp-008 to exp-011 |\n130\t| Confusability measure validity | Embedding ablation (D010) + pairwise vs per-type analysis | D010, exp-015 |\n131\t| Effect size small | Pairwise r=0.12-0.16 + FewRel Δ=21-50pp + confusion ratio 10-28x | multiple |\n132\t| MAVEN per-type opposite | Centrality confound analysis; pairwise still works | MAVEN MiniLM |\n133\t| Embedding choice matters? | 2×3 ablation table; SDGD-cal bypasses embedding entirely | D010 |\n134\t| Why not per-type splitting? | SDGD vs per-type vs random ablation | exp-013, exp-014 |\n135\t| Latency overhead | Report API calls and wall-clock time | exp-008 |\n136\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d7a5a19-b1bd-4793-b072-30ea1d0ec2fd","uuid":"98645f88-c44e-49e7-bb3c-dd70cfe6f50c","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:16:18.842Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_18/projects/schema-dag-extraction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T113743/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — schema-dag-extraction\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 cycle)\n- Commitment deadline: August 2, 2026\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings (same ARR cycle, commitment August 26)\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (10 days from today)\n\n## Core Claims (3 conditions) — Revised per D012\n\n1. **Confusability Independence**: Type confusability independently predicts extraction quality degradation in training-free LLM IE, beyond what type count alone explains. The signal is strongest and most robust at the **type-pair level** (pairwise SCS → confusion), validated across NER (Few-NERD), RE (FewRel), and ED (MAVEN with MiniLM). Per-type aggregation (mean BCS) introduces a centrality confound in semantically homogeneous schemas. Evidence required: (a) significant pairwise SCS-confusion correlation on >=2 datasets, (b) extreme-batch accuracy gap on FewRel, (c) >=2 models.\n\n2. **Multi-Channel Degradation**: Count and confusability degrade extraction through orthogonal channels -- count causes entity omission (recall decline), while confusability causes type confusion errors (correct spans labeled with wrong types). Evidence required: error taxonomy showing differential error types per channel, monotonic trends in separate metrics.\n\n3. **SDGD Effectiveness**: Confusability-aware schema decomposition (SDGD) -- partitioning types into low-confusability batches via graph coloring on the pairwise-similarity-thresholded graph -- yields significant F1 gains over single-pass and heuristic decomposition on complex schemas (>=30 types). SDGD directly leverages pairwise confusability (validated signal), avoiding per-type aggregation confounds. Evidence required: SDGD > single-pass, SDGD > random batching (same k), SDGD >= per-type splitting (with lower latency).\n\n## Story Spine — Revised per D012\n\n- **Problem**: Training-free LLM IE degrades severely on complex schemas (20-60 F1 gap vs supervised). All existing decomposition approaches operate on unvalidated assumptions about WHAT makes schemas complex for LLMs.\n\n- **Existing approaches & their gaps**: UniNER splits per-type (gains 3.3 F1 but loses cross-type context, no criterion for when to split). LLM-PEE uses similarity as implicit confusability proxy (never validated empirically). No prior work isolates confusability from count, or characterizes when aggregated confusability measures lose signal.\n\n- **Our framing**: We conduct the first controlled empirical study isolating type confusability from type count in training-free LLM IE across three tasks (NER, RE, ED). We discover: (1) a multi-channel degradation model (count→recall, confusability→type confusion), (2) pairwise type confusability is a robust cross-task signal, (3) per-type aggregation of confusability is confounded by type centrality in homogeneous schemas. We operationalize pairwise confusability into SDGD, a principled framework for confusability-minimizing schema decomposition.\n\n- **Three-task validation**:\n  - NER (Few-NERD, 66 types, cross-domain): Pairwise r=0.156 (p<1e-11), per-type ρ=-0.293 (p=0.02), 10-28x confusion ratio\n  - RE (FewRel, 80 relations, cross-domain): Extreme-batch accuracy gap Δ=21-50pp\n  - ED (MAVEN, 168 event types, same-domain): Pairwise MiniLM r=0.120 (p≈0); per-type positive (centrality confound case study)\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"Pairwise type confusability independently predicts extraction degradation across NER, RE, and ED tasks (r=0.12-0.16, p<1e-6), with 10-28x more type confusion errors in high-confusability batches. On semantically homogeneous schemas, per-type aggregation obscures the signal through centrality confounding, but pairwise confusability remains valid. SDGD-zero, operating on pairwise similarity, improves F1 by X points over single-pass on Few-NERD.\"\n\n## Core Insight — Multi-Channel Degradation + Pairwise Robustness\n\nSchema-induced degradation in LLM IE is not a single phenomenon but a multi-channel process:\n- **Channel 1 (Count -> Recall)**: More types in the prompt → attention dilution → entities missed. Monotonic, near-linear. Addressable by reducing batch size.\n- **Channel 2 (Confusability -> Type Confusion)**: Semantically similar co-present types → interference during type assignment → correct entities labeled with wrong types. Addressable by separating confusable types into different batches.\n\nThese channels are orthogonal and independently addressable.\n\n**Pairwise vs Aggregated Confusability**:\n- **Pairwise confusability** (SCS between type pairs) is robust across all tasks and schema types. Validated on Few-NERD (Qwen3, r=0.156) and MAVEN (MiniLM, r=0.120).\n- **Per-type aggregation** (mean BCS = average pairwise similarity to all other types) introduces a centrality confound: in semantically homogeneous schemas (MAVEN), types with many semantic neighbors are central, well-represented types that LLMs extract well → positive correlation (high mean BCS → high F1), masking the pairwise confusability signal.\n- **SDGD operates at pairwise level**, directly using the validated signal to construct the confusability graph for decomposition. It avoids the aggregation confound entirely.\n\n## Evidence Hierarchy (D012)\n\n### Tier 1: PRIMARY — Pairwise SCS → Confusion\n\nThe cleanest evidence. Directly measures: are semantically similar type pairs more often confused?\n\n**Few-NERD (NER)** — Qwen3 embeddings:\n- Pearson r=0.156 (p=4.6e-12, n=1953 type pairs)\n- Nonzero-only Spearman ρ=0.254 (p=1.1e-6)\n- Top confused pairs are all high-BCS semantic neighbors (person-other ↔ person-politician, BCS=0.934)\n- Immune to type frequency confound (operates at type-pair level)\n\n**MAVEN (ED)** — MiniLM embeddings:\n- Pearson r=+0.120 (p≈0, n=11026 type pairs)\n- Nonzero-only Spearman ρ=+0.191 (p<0.001)\n- Cross-task replication on same-domain schema\n- Note: Qwen3 pairwise not significant on MAVEN (r=-0.007, p=0.41) — embedding choice matters for pairwise signal in homogeneous schemas\n\n### Tier 2: STRONG SECONDARY — FewRel Extreme-Batch Comparison\n\nLarge effect size, cross-task (RE), intuitive demonstration:\n- count_4: low-BCS 91.7% vs high-BCS 70.8% (Δ=-20.9pp)\n- count_8: low-BCS 100% vs high-BCS 50.0% (Δ=-50.0pp)\n- count_16: low-BCS 91.7% vs high-BCS 43.1% (Δ=-48.6pp)\n- Effect increases with count — consistent with multi-channel model\n- MiniLM embeddings; pending: Qwen3 formal study\n\n### Tier 3: SUPPORTING — Few-NERD Per-type Analysis\n\nBridges pairwise and batch-level, demonstrates per-type signal in cross-domain schema:\n- Spearman ρ=-0.293 (p=0.020, n=63 types, freq≥5) — Qwen3 embeddings\n- Partial r=-0.200 (p=0.116) controlling for log-frequency\n- Quartile comparison: high-BCS types F1=0.228 vs low-BCS F1=0.310 (Δ=-8.2pp)\n- BCS-frequency uncorrelated at type level (r=0.042, p=0.74)\n- MiniLM per-type: ρ≈0 (p=0.97) — extraction model alignment required for per-type signal\n\n### Tier 4: DISCUSSION — MAVEN Per-type Centrality Confound\n\nMethodological case study on when aggregated confusability measures fail:\n- Qwen3 per-type: ρ=+0.189 (p=0.021) — OPPOSITE direction\n- MiniLM per-type: ρ=+0.208 (p=0.011) — ALSO positive, ruling out embedding compression as sole explanation\n- Both embeddings agree: positive direction on MAVEN is an intrinsic property of the type structure\n- Explanation: in homogeneous schemas, mean BCS conflates confusability with type centrality (types with many semantic neighbors → common/central types → higher F1)\n- This is stronger than \"domain boundary\" — it identifies the specific mechanism (aggregation confound) rather than just the boundary condition\n\n### Tier 5: MECHANISTIC — Error Taxonomy\n\nConfusion rate differential demonstrates the mechanism:\n- Extreme batches: high-BCS 10-28x more type confusion errors vs low-BCS\n- Random batches: 1.7-2.4x ratio (still significant, smaller effect)\n- Type confusion errors increase with count AND with confusability (additive)\n\n## Embedding Ablation (D010)\n\n2×3 matrix: {Qwen3, MiniLM} × {Few-NERD, FewRel, MAVEN}\n\n### Per-type (Layer 2)\n| | Few-NERD | FewRel | MAVEN |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Qwen3 | ρ=-0.293 ✓ | pending | ρ=+0.189 ✗ |\n| MiniLM | ρ≈0 ✗ | Δ=21-50pp ✓ | ρ=+0.208 ✗ |\n\n### Pairwise (Layer 1)\n| | Few-NERD | MAVEN |\n|---|---|---|\n| Qwen3 | r=0.156 ✓ | r=-0.007 ✗ |\n| MiniLM | — | r=+0.120 ✓ |\n\n**Interpretation**: No single embedding dominates. Extraction-model embeddings (Qwen3) capture per-type confusability in cross-domain schemas. Generic embeddings (MiniLM) capture pairwise confusability in same-domain schemas. SDGD should use task-appropriate embeddings; SDGD-cal (empirical confusion) bypasses embedding choice entirely.\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **\"Just an empirical study\"**: Mitigated by SDGD as direct operationalization. Controlled experimental design parallels \"Lost in the Middle\" (TACL 2024).\n- **Training-free IE relevance**: Cite deployment scenarios — clinical, regulatory, multilingual.\n- **Multi-model generalizability**: Qwen3-32B primary + LLaMA-3.3-70B (exp-012).\n- **MAVEN doesn't support hypothesis?**: Pairwise MiniLM does support it. Per-type centrality confound is methodological contribution, not failure.\n- **Embedding sensitivity**: 2×3 ablation matrix is itself a contribution — characterizes when which proxy works.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n| Concern | Response Strategy | Experiment |\n|---------|------------------|------------|\n| Only one model | LLaMA-3.3-70B replication | exp-012 |\n| Cross-task replication | Pairwise: Few-NERD ✓ + MAVEN MiniLM ✓. Batch: FewRel ✓. Three tasks. | exp-002, exp-004, fewrel |\n| No practical method | SDGD framework (-zero, -cal) | exp-008 to exp-011 |\n| Confusability measure validity | Embedding ablation (D010) + pairwise vs per-type analysis | D010, exp-015 |\n| Effect size small | Pairwise r=0.12-0.16 + FewRel Δ=21-50pp + confusion ratio 10-28x | multiple |\n| MAVEN per-type opposite | Centrality confound analysis; pairwise still works | MAVEN MiniLM |\n| Embedding choice matters? | 2×3 ablation table; SDGD-cal bypasses embedding entirely | D010 |\n| Why not per-type splitting? | SDGD vs per-type vs random ablation | exp-013, exp-014 |\n| Latency overhead | Report API calls and wall-clock time | exp-008 |\n","numLines":136,"startLine":1,"totalLines":136}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011EnNWAw8Y4EsK1gy6kjjUK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the experiment data and the paper framing. Let me now write the LaTeX paper according to the \"worst\" tier narrative guidance:\n\nKey narrative direction:\n- Completely abandon SDGD as a method contribution\n- Reframe as a pure systematic empirical analysis\n- Schema complexity is not one-dimensional — count and confusability degrade performance through orthogonal channels\n- Confusability signal is highly dependent on model and embedding choice\n- Pairwise confusability is more robust than per-type aggregation, but only significant in specific model×embedding×schema combinations\n- Centrality confound is itself a methodological contribution\n\n\n- Model-specific effects show that confusability patterns vary significantly across architectures like Qwen3 and LLaMA, which I'll frame as a key finding rather than a limitation\n- The paper will follow a question-driven structure moving from controlled experiments to findings and their implications, with SDGD relegated to a negative result appendix\n\nNow I need to systematically cover all seven experiments: the MAVEN and DocRED confusability studies, the count-confusability interaction, the error taxonomy binned by confusability scores, the LLaMA validation across models, and the two SDGD-zero ablations on Few-NERD and MAVEN.\n\nFor the remaining experiments—SDGD-cal variants, random batching ablation, per-type splitting comparison, embedding validation against empirical confusion, and the cross-experiment summary—I'll integrate these into the findings sections to show how different training approaches and data organization strategies either amplify or mitigate the confusability effect.\n\nThe paper will open with the core question about schema complexity, establish the experimental setup with tasks and metrics, then present findings progressively: first showing that pairwise confusability predicts type confusion in a model-dependent way, then demonstrating that count and confusability operate through distinct mechanisms, and finally synthesizing how these insights apply across different training paradigms. I'm mapping out where each experiment fits into the paper structure—most of the SDGD variants belong in an appendix as negative result case studies rather than core contributions, but I still need dedicated sections or tables for every experiment in the data file. Now I'm ready to start writing the full paper using a standard neuroscience conference format.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23010,"cache_read_input_tokens":23153,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23010},"output_tokens":12,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d7a5a19-b1bd-4793-b072-30ea1d0ec2fd","uuid":"69d2c775-2a66-4589-b9a6-0a7d982f34ea"}
